1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Dahlpihl, Beata Persdotter'''
2 CONT * * c. 1690
2 CONT * oo 1715
2 CONT * † 1759-05-15, as "69 years of age"
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Wedded at a camp for Svea artilleriregemente''' ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artilleriregementet_%28old%29 Artilleriregementet (old)]) in [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roslagen Roslagen], Sweden. Very little else is known abo
2 CONC ut Beata and her side of the family, a signature appearing alongside her husbands probate (Swedish: ''bouppteckning'') hints at the assumption that she could write.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shared ancestry with ''Petter Dahlpihl'', rider for no. 84 Skåra, Stigtomta between 1684 and 1705, Backman (1995, 262) writes that the connection is likely though it has not been possible to verify. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 255, 263.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT * The name ''Dahlpihl'' is not a common one, but was used as a soldiers name and probably takes a joking aim at the crossed arrows on the 1-[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96re öre] coins available at the time (or at the [http:/
2 CONC /en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalarna Coat of Arms of Dalarna]).
