2 _MARNM Nyman
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1706
1 OCCU Skipper, Boatswain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nyman, Peter Carlsson'''
2 CONT * † 1706.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Was a skipper and a boatswain'''. Very little is known about this line of the Nyman's since documentation is lacking, making valid statements about identities very difficult. What is known is that Peter died 1706 (possibly due 
2 CONC to the war) and that he before this point also had a small farm on Tavastgatan in Stockholm, Sweden—an area where also other skippers, sailors and commoners lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Anbytarforum, s.v. “[http://aforum.genealogi.se/discus/messages/83331/11006.html Lenin, Vladimir Ilich Uljanov]” (accessed March 1, 2012).
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 255.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes'''
2 CONT * Tavastgatan: Taweste giathan 1649, Tavaste gathun 1650, Tavastg[atan] 1820, is a part of the oldest layers of street names on [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6dermalm Södermalm], aka Söder, in Stockholm, Sweden. The word tav
2 CONC aste '' 'tavastalänning' '' has earlier been used as a so called ''tillnamn'' or ''binamn'' (i.e. "Pepin ''the Short'' " etc.) in Stockholm.
