3 CITY Kristinehamn
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Glover, handskmakare
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Östedt, Carl Reinhold'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * * c. 1714.
2 CONT * oo 1740-07-03.
2 CONT * [ ] 1748-03-13.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Born in Livonia c. 1714. In 1730, at 16 years of age, he was a glover apprentice''' (Swedish: ''handskmakarlärling'') with Johan Ditzinger in Stockholm, Sweden and later as a journeyman (Swedish: ''gesäll'') in 1740 with Fredri
2 CONC k Linzell. C.R.Ö. came to Uppsala 1741, now a master in his profession. He accidentally shot himself while cleaning a pistol and was unable to perform his craft satisfactory during his final years because of the pain inflicted by 
2 CONC the cleaning scraper (Swedish: ''kratsmoder'') that was still stuck in his back. Backman (1995) also mentions that it's in all likelyhood the very same Carl, being on a trip to ''Fastingsmarknaden'' in Kristinehamn, who was the "t
2 CONC he stranger" that died and was also buried there in 1748-03-13.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References / Notes'''
