1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Östedt, Carolina Gustava'''
2 CONT * * 1779-02-23
2 CONT * ~ 1779-02-26
2 CONT * c. 1782 to Saint Petersburg, Russia
2 CONT * † after 1860
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Governess for the landholder Topornin's nine chldren''' in Ufa, Russia, and later on ditto for her early deceased niece Anna Blanks children (i.e. [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Ivanovna-Grosschopff/6000000010019081631 ''Anna
2 CONC  Ivanovna Grosschopff'']). Born in Stockholm, Sweden, Carolina first came to the growing metropolis Saint Petersburg as a three year old, together with her family. Died after 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Backman (1995:258)''' explains that the cousins [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Lovisa-Borg/6000000011288023882 Anna Lovisa Borg] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Beata-%C3%96stedt/6000000010020016420 Anna Beata Östedt] in
2 CONC  Saint Petersburg ‘married German’ but that it was through the latter, and specifically through her sister―the governess Carolina Gustava―that the usage of the Swedish language was preserved in the family for later generations. St
2 CONC ill Lenin's sister [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Ilyinichna-Ulyanova/6000000010031350550 Maria] was able to write letters using good Swedish.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References / Notes'''
