2 CONT
2 CONT '''Grosschopff, Johann Gottlieb'''
2 CONT * ~ 1766-03-09. (Backman 1995)
2 CONT * * 1766-03-09. (Kruse in Renner 2008)
2 CONT * oo 1793-03-12
2 CONT * † 1817 (Kruse 2007)
2 CONT * † c. 1822. (Kruse in Renner 2008)
2 CONT * † c. 1845. (Backman 1995)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Had a large library and violin collection'''. Born in Lübeck, Germany and baptized in the Lübeck Cathedral (''Dom zu Lübeck, Lübecker Dom'') in 1766-03-09. He was a businessman and a merchant. Temporary secretary of the provinc
2 CONC ial administration and later a notary public in St. Petersburg (German: ''Verwaltung Gouvernementssekretär'' & ''Volksnotar''). Emigrated to Saint Petersburg, Russia 1790. J.G.G. was also the director of the company ''Friedrich Sc
2 CONC hade & Co. — Фридрих Шаде и К.°'' in Saint Petersburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p.264.
