1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Måns'''
2 CONT
2 CONT […] ''' “the first bridegroom is''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Per-M%C3%A5nsson/6000000011082291998 Per Månsson], who's [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-M%C3%A5ns-Persson-Borg/6000000011240037703 oldest son] is born a year afte
2 CONC r the wedding, and according to old customs is named Måns after his [paternal] grandfather (Swedish: ''farfar'') and takes the name Borg, after the farm Borghult.” (Backman 1995, 257). Backman also goes on to explain that the poss
2 CONC ibility to identify the brothers' [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-M%C3%A5ns-Persson-Borg/6000000011240037703 Magnus], [http://www.geni.com/people/Nils-Persson-Borg/6000000011240039181 Nils] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Carl-
2 CONC Persson-Borg/6000000010033111563 Carl Borg]'s maternal and paternal grandparents with a 100% certainty is seemingly not to doable. The names ''[http://www.geni.com/people/Knut/6000000011082654453 Knut]'' and ''Måns'' were common i
2 CONC n Vimmerby, and patronymicon were seldom used in church or official records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 257.
