2 CONT
2 CONT Yo Uppsalassa 3.3.1758 Erik Borg U803. * 3.1.1738. Säämiskäntekijän poika Strängnäsistä. Strängnäsin koulun oppilas. Strängnäsin lukion oppilas 1749/50. Ylioppilas Uppsalassa 3.3.1758 Ericus Borg Sud. (* 1738). — Työskennellyt Kos
2 CONC mografisen seuran palveluksessa Uppsalassa. Turun akatemian kaivertaja 1765. † Tukholmassa alkuvuodesta 1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Borg, Erik'''
2 CONT * * 1737-01-04
2 CONT * † 1767-02-05
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colored the ''Icones Insectorum Rariorum'' ''' together with C. M. Rising for the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Sciences Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences]. Student with the engraver Anders Åkerman. In 
2 CONC 1764-10-26 Erik was proposed and appointed engraver at Åbo Akademi (i.e. [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Academy_of_%C3%85bo Regia Academia Aboensis]) in 1765, where he seemingly did not serve. Before this, Erik finished the t
2 CONC rivium (Swedish: ''trivialskola'') at 1750-06-09 and was a student at the gymnasium between 1750-1758. Enrolled at Uppsala University and [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6dermanlands-Nerikes_nation Södermanlands-Nerikes nation
2 CONC ] in 1758-03-03.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 269.
