1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Bertilsson, Erik'''
2 CONT * * c. 1620.
2 CONT * ooI before 1654.
2 CONT * ooII before 1658.
2 CONT * [ ] 1683-03-18.
2 CONT
2 CONT Is the ''likely'' son of Bertil Jönsson. Backman (1995) lists two more children of Bertil, siblings to Erik, both NN and buried in Arboga, Sweden 1651-09-16 and 1653. The maternity of those two is unclear. Though, since Erik was b
2 CONC orn around 1620, it is here ‘assumed’ that he originates from the first marrige. That is, ''if'' Bertil is his father at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bourgeois in Arboga 1638-07-03 as a skipper'''. Adultery (Swedish: ''lägersmål'') with Brita Larsdotter 1641-11-25 (Backman 1995, 264). Merchant and skipper in Västerås from c. 1654, became blind during his latter years. Buried
2 CONC  in Västerås at 1683-03-18 as "63 years old".
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 256, 264.
