1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''NN, Jacob'''
2 CONT * ~ 1666-09-25, Västerås, Sweden.
2 CONT * † before 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Was put through schooling to become a ''sämskmakare'' ''' (Also in Swedish: ''garvning'', English: ''tanning''). Letter to the "shammy-guild" 1683-10-03 (Swedish: ''bördsbrev till sämskmakarämbetet''). A sämskmakare worked with
2 CONC  [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamois_leather chamois leather], aka ''shammy'', producing gloves etc. During Jacob's days in Sweden, the preferred hide providers were deer, reindeer, moose, sheep, goats but also cattle in general
2 CONC  for a rougher and coarser end-produce.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT * Backman, Christina. “Lenins svenska anor.” ''Släkt och Hävd'' №1 (1995): 253–273, p. 256, 265.
