1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Бланк, Абель Мошевич''' — '''Blank, Abel Moishevich'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * * 1794.
2 CONT * ~ 1820-07-10. Blank, Dmitrii Dmitrievich.
2 CONT * † 1831-06-26.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Both Abel and his brother [http://www.geni.com/people/Srul-Moishevich-Blank/6000000010019232673 Srul] went to Saint Petersburg'''and were baptized in the Orthodox Christianity, hence '''Abel Moishevich Blank''' became '''Dmitri
2 CONC i Dmitrievich Blank'''. The baptism took place in the Samson Cathedral, in Saint Petersburg's Vyborg district. The godfathers were senator Dmitry Baranov and the privy councillor, count Aleksandr Ivanovich Apraksin. From the forme
2 CONC r they also got their new patronymic. This circumstance allowed them into the Saint Petersburg Medico-Surgical Academy in 1820, from which they graduated four years later. Dmitrii died during a cholera riot in 1831.
2 CONT
