1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vladimir Ilyich Ulyanov''' (alias '''Lenin''') was a Russian communist revolutionary, politician and political theorist. He served as head of government of the Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic from 1
2 CONC 917, and of the Soviet Union from 1922 until his death. Under his administration, the Russian Empire was replaced by the Soviet Union; all wealth including land, industry and business was nationalized. Based in Marxism, his politi
2 CONC cal theories are known as Leninism.
2 CONT
2 CONT * * 1870-04-10 O.S.
2 CONT * * 1870-04-22 N.S.
2 CONT * ~ 1870-04-16 O.S.
2 CONT * ~ 1870-04-28 N.S.
2 CONT * oo 1898-07-10 O.S.
2 CONT * oo 1898-07-22 N.S.
2 CONT * † 1924-01-21  N.S. 18:50 hrs, Moscow Time.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Was a revolutionary''', an organizer of Bolshevism, a Marxist theorist, communist politician, statesman and the founder of the Soviet Union.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Baptized in St. Nicholas Cathedral, Simbirsk, Russia''' at 1870-04-28. The godparents were Arseni Belokrysenko, an accountant in the civil administration, also [http://www.geni.com/people/Ilya-Nikolayevich-Ulyanov/6000000010018
2 CONC 994260 Ilya]'s chesspartner, and Natalya Aunovska, a widowed mother of one of Ilya's colleagues.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1898, Lenin lived the deportee's dream''' and married [http://www.geni.com/people/Nadezhda-Konstantinovna-Krupskaya/6000000010018544860 Nadezhda Krupskaya] in Siberia where both had been in exile at the time. They had no chi
2 CONC ldren. The two had met about seven years prior.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1917-04-13 09:23''', arrives in Stockholm, Sweden. During the day he procures a pair of sturdy shoes, a pair of pants and an ovecoat from [http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pub_%28varuhus%29 PUB], a major department store in the cit
2 CONC y. Departs from Stockholm 18:37 in the evening.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lenin survived an assassination attempt in August 1918. In April 1922 one of the bullets was extracted from his neck.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a series of strokes, Lenin died 1924-01-21. His last testament was concealed until 1956.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alias'''
2 CONT * ''Ilich'' — Respectful nickname for Lenin, used mainly inside the party.
2 CONT * ''Lenin'' — The most famous of the 160 pseudonyms he used. He adopted the pseudonym during his underground party work after his exile in Siberia. The word Lenin is believed to have been derived from the Russian river Lena.
2 CONT * ''Vladimir Ilich'' — Lenin's Christian name and patronymic.
2 CONT * ''Vladimir Ilich Ulyanov'' — Lenin's name at his christening.
2 CONT * ''Volodya'' — The diminutive of Lenin's first name.
2 CONT * ''N. Lenin'' — Sometimes, Vladimir signed with N. Lenin. People filled the gap in their minds and Nikolai, a common Russian name, was invented.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
