1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Улья́нова, Мари́я Ильи́нична''' — '''Ulyanova, Maria Ilyinichna'''
2 CONT >Wikipedia: [http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A3%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%8F%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0,_%D0%9C%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%8F_%D0%98%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B0 ru]
2 CONT * * 1878-02-06 O.S.
2 CONT * * 1878-02-18 N.S.
2 CONT * † 1937-06-12 N.S.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Backman (1995:258)''' explains that the cousins [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Lovisa-Borg/6000000011288023882 Anna Lovisa Borg] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Beata-%C3%96stedt/6000000010020016420 Anna Beata Östedt] in
2 CONC  Saint Petersburg ‘married German’ but that it was through the latter, and specifically through her sister―the governess [http://www.geni.com/people/Carolina-Gustava-%C3%96stedt/6000000011077874825 Carolina Gustava]―that the usage
2 CONC  of the Swedish language was preserved in the family for later generations. Still Lenin's sister Maria was able to write letters using good Swedish.
2 CONT
