1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Alice Ellis Burchard Ruhl (Grosschopff )''' was born on August 4, 1903 in Waballen, Riga, Latvia. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34697231526 Eugen Edmund von Grosschopff] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-346972
2 CONC 32126 Hedwig Henriette von Grosschopff]. She was a Business Owner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis Alice married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927154 Harold Burchard, I]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927155 Harold Burchard, II];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740391029 Manfred Nils Burchard]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis Alice married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34697296552 Joseph Ruhl] in 1952 in Bremen, HB, Germany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on March 18, 1988, in Lafayette, Lafayette Parish, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/125133382#]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Her family had an idyllic life in Riga, Latvia, changed drastically after their family lived in the county for Centuries. When World War II broke out,  Soviet troops came in and forced them to leave; they were forced out of Latvia
2 CONC , leaving behind their large estate home, business, art collection, jewelry most all clothing.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT On January 24, 1945, on the way to Bremen, German, they were in Gotenhafen, Pomerania, Poland. She, as well as her young sons, witnessed her husband shot in the streets by Polish Partisans. The next day she and her son's continued
2 CONC  to Germany to live with relatives. She was forced to be a hotel maid to feed her children and live with relatives, not the station in life she was born to, but adjusted to as many displaced families during the war with no options
2 CONC , as they left behind all of their fortunes in Latvia. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She immigrated to America in 1952 after meeting an American and re-marrying; her youngest son was 17 yrs old. He finished high school in New Orleans, LA, USA, and then attend LSU. Her son, Manfred, became a geo-physicist and, over
2 CONC  the years, worked for various oil companies, including Shell and Tenneco. He became successful as did she; she owned a Chevrolet car dealership in New Orleans, LA, and many investment properties in Texas and Louisianna, USA.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She was a gracious person and well respected. We were proud to have her as a part of our family as well. What can you say about a sweet soul who saw her young husband shot in front of herself and her young children? After this tra
2 CONC gedy, you would never know she was born and brought up in luxury, never complaining, but working hard to become successful in business.  When she remarried and moved to America, the man she married was abusive, she bravely separat
2 CONC ed but didn't divorce him; they were Catholic. She worked during the day as a secretary and went to school at night to finish her degree in business and become proficient in the English language. Her husband died after they separa
2 CONC ted.  After his death never married again, she spent her years working as a Legal Assistant,  buying rental properties and managing them. She was a wonderful mother and grandmother. I loved and respected her Suzan Martin 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
