3 CTRY Russland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 JAN 1945
2 ADDR
3 CITY Gotenhafen
3 CTRY Poland
1 OCCU Kaufmann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Harald Burchard, I'''  born on October 2, 1902 in Rīga, Kreis Riga / Рижский уезд, Лифляндская губерния, Российская империя. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34695211179 Alfred Alexander Burchard] and [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/profile-34695211194 Selina Burchard]. He was a Kaufmann/ Merchant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927153 Alice Ellis Burchard Ruhl (Grosschopff )] circa 1927 in Riga, Latvia. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927155 Harold Burchard, II]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740391029 Manfred Nils Burchard]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on January 24, 1945, in Gotenhafen, Poland from ermordet/English, Gunshot and buried in Gotenhafen [http://www.zck.pl/historia_witominski/]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- He was a wonderful father who died on January 24, 1945, in Gotenhafen, Pomerania, Poland.  He was shot in the streets by Polish Partisans, trying to protect his wife and children. Harald Burchard,  as well as his family, befo
2 CONC re that day, had an idyllic life in Riga, Latvia. The Burchard and von Grosschoff family lived in the county for Centuries until World War II and the Soviet Army invasion forced the German and German Jewish Citizens out of Latvia.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald did not want to fight the war for the German Nazi Regime. He was killed before he made it to Germany, The Burchard Family were a family without a county. They were Lavatian's for centuries. They were caught in a horrific de
2 CONC adly War on the wrong side, they lost several family members that were executed by Hitler's Regime. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT My father and grandmother did not return to Riga until the 1970s, it was a bittersweet memory for them to walk the streets that had so many happy memories before January 1945. They lost most of their family to the War, their home,
2 CONC  the centuries of family heirlooms, portraits, priceless art collections, their estate, money. One of the sisters had the few photographs we have posted. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The saddest part of all is what the holocaust directly did was to scar so many souls. His youngest son, Manfred was 10 yrs old when all of this came crumbling down around him. He saw his father shot in the streets, for nothing oth
2 CONC er than protecting his young wife and children. He witnesses Jewish children being mistreated and he didn't understand why.  The Jewish people were their friends. They were Lavians, they spoke Baltic and Russian as the first langu
2 CONC age rather than German, German was 2nd to 3rd language. He spent his life reading everything he could to try to grasp what happened. It always brought tears to Manfred's eyes. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''References''' [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000137297774836&] Official Record, his wife gave the report at headquarters in Germany once they arrived in safety with relatives. 
2 CONT
