1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Harold Burchard, II''' was born on June 18, 1929, in Rīga, Latvija. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927154 Harold Burchard, I] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927153 Ellis Alice Sophie Burchard]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 7, 1958, in Berlin, Berlin, Germany from He was hit by a car while riding a bicycle, hit and run.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Harald Burchard, II  as well as his family, before that day, had an idyllic life in Riga, Latvia. The Burchard and von Grosschoff family lived in the county for Centuries until World War II and the Soviet Army invasion forced
2 CONC  the German and German Jewish Citizens out of Latvia. His father was shot trying to protect his family on January 24, 1945, in Gotenhafen, Pomerania, Poland while they were on their way to Bremen, Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744927154 Harold Burchard, I]  did not want to fight the war for the German Nazi Regime. He was killed before he made it to Germany, The Burchard Family were a family without a county. Th
2 CONC ey were Lavatian's for centuries. They were caught in a horrific deadly War on the wrong side, they lost several family members that were executed by Hitler's Regime.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Harald Burchard was very outspoken against the Nazi regime and the treatment of the Jewish people during the war.  His brother Manfred, his friends and family warned him to be careful about what he said and who he spoke to du
2 CONC ring and after the war. He didn't care.   
2 CONT
2 CONT His family worried for his safety, after his uncle's death. They always believed his death was no accident, the weather was nice the day of the accident and he was riding on a bike path and not the road. They firmly thought his un
2 CONC derground work during WWII assisting people and his outspoken ways lead to his untimely death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He didn't immigrate to America from Germany with his mother and younger brother when she re-married to an American man she met in Bremen, Germany. He stayed in Germany; he was a graduate student at Berlin University with a great j
2 CONC ob at the time. Sadly, his mother and brother received news by telephone about the accident and his death. For many years Manfred investigated his death and hired a private investigator to no avail. 
2 CONT ----
