1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Ruth Martin Burchard (Stephens)''' was born on January 27, 1929, in Austin, Travis County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34712167592 James Edgar Stephens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile
2 CONC -34715857540 Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34709266809 Henry Victor Martin, II] on April 6, 1947, in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States. Together they had three children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716542291 Ira Lee Martin]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716539242 Vicki Martin Hester, Ph.D.]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34708696546 Suzan Martin].
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740390858 Cyrill Ferrall] on June 22, 1974, he died: August 14, 1978, of cancer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740391029 Manfred Nils Burchard] in June of 1980 in Lafayette, Lafayette Parish, LA, United States, he died of heart failure April 06, 2010.   
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on September 15, 2013, in Houston, Harris County, Texas, the United States from Heart Failure, Alzheimer's, and was buried in Norwood Cemetery, Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States. Reference: [https://www.finda
2 CONC grave.com/memorial/119676237/ruth-stephens-martin Find A Grave Memorial] -  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Her Occupation; Musician, Elementary Music Teacher, Church Organist, Pianist, Piano Teacher
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/36151787/the_hearne_democrat/] Evidently, our mother was a Southern Baptist before she married my father, yet my siblings and I were always were members of the Episcopalian Church all of ou
2 CONC r lives. We knew our paternal grandparents were Methodist. Interesting I just discovered this when I found the wedding announcement. I always assumed they married at Grace Methodist in Hearne, TX because my Uncle Carr Peel married
2 CONC  them, this we knew for a fact. 
2 CONT
2 CONT {{[https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000064138915859?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000103900867065&position=0{}}{}}] The Gold Bracelet our Treasured Tradition, Its mentioned in my mother's wedding announcement.   We enjoy
2 CONC ed wearing one of the old bracelets of our 2nd Great-grandmother " Mary "Molly" Rebecca Lancaster Trigg wore, Suzan Martin 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ruth Gene Martin Stephens''' was born January 27, 1929, in Austin, Travis County, Texas to parents James Edgar Stephens and Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster). She attended Sam Houston State College, Huntsville, Texas until she
2 CONC  met Henry Victor Martin, Jr. after he returned from World War II, they were married April 6, 1947, in Hearne, Texas. he was the son of Henry Victor Martin Sr. and Lena Clementine Martin (Moseley).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Martin were communicants of St. Philips Episcopal Church where Mr. Martin served as a member of the Vestry and Mrs. Martin was active in the Church School and as the church organist. He was a member of the Miles Scriv
2 CONC ener American Legions Post of Hearne, a former member of the Hearne Rotary Club, and was very active in the work of Cub Scouting with his son. After her husband's death, May 5, 1960, Ruth returned to College in Huntsville, Texas t
2 CONC o complete her Bachelor of Music degree and taught Elementary Music until her retirement in 1985. After he graduated from Sam Houston State in Huntsville, Texas she moved with her children to Houston, Texas on January 1964. 
2 CONT
