2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Henry Victor Martin, Jr.''' was born on July 23, 1924, in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34711975132 Henry Victor Martin, Sr] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-347
2 CONC 14737853 Lena Clementine Moseley]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34709266998 Ruth Gene Martin] on April 6, 1947, in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716542291 Ira Lee Martin]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716539242 Vicki Martin Hester, Ph.D.]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34708696546 Suzan Martin]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on Ma,y 9, 1960 in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States and was buried in 1960 in Norwood Cemetery. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''' Henry Victor Martin, Jr,''' was born July 23, 1924, in Hearne, Texas, his father, Henry Victor Martin, Sr. was 32 and his mother, Lena Clementine Martin (Moseley), was 28. He had two sisters; Frances Katherine Putz (Martin) an
2 CONC d Margaret Moseley Lumpkin (Martin).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Victor Martin, Jr''' married   Ruth Gene Stephens on April 6, 1947, in Hearne, Texas. She was the daughter of James Edgar Stephens and Julia Eugenia Stephens(Lancaster) of Hearne, Texas. Three children were born to Mr. an
2 CONC d Mrs. Martin:
2 CONT * Ira Lee Martin, April 5, 1948
2 CONT * Dr. Vicki Gene Hester (Martin), January 10, 1951
2 CONT * Suzan Martin October 6, 1954.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended Hearne public schools and was graduated from Hearne High School with the Class of 1942. He then enlisted in the U. S. Army where he served for thirty-four months during World War II, his overseas duty being in Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He returned to Hearne in the latter part of 1945 after being discharged from military duty. He began the operation of Martin's Dry Cleaning business in February 1946, located on Magnolia Street in Hearne, a business that previousl
2 CONC y was established and operated by his father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT .Mr. and Mrs. Martin were communicants of St. Philips Episcopal Church where Mr. Martin served as a member of the Vestry and Mrs. Martin was active in the Church School and as the church organist. He was a member of the Miles Scri
2 CONC vener American Legions Post of Hearne, a former member of the Hearne Rotary Club, and was very active in the work of Cub Scouting with his son. He also taught Sunday School Class at St. Phillips.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Victor Martin, Jr. served with the US Army QM Railhead Co he was in Special Forces, was an engineer sent in with a few men sent in with explosives to destroy bridges during WWII.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought on April 28, 1944, Operation Tiger. During this battle, he was injured and lived with two bullets on the sides of his spine, not found until about one year before his death in 1960! He lived in unspeakable pain. By the t
2 CONC ime he was rescued from the water, the doctors at the hospital in the UK thought and treated him for flesh wounds.  The VA told him all those years it was nerves from the war causing pain. An X-Ray showed the bullets he carried al
2 CONC l those years. He died one day in a small town hospital before he was to be transported to Houston VA Hospital to remove the bullets pressing on his spine causing the pain. The death was an accidental overdose of pain medicine by 
2 CONC hospital staff. So, he lived in pain every day since the day his ship was hit by torpedoes from the German E-Boat. He was a wonderful father and is missed by everyone. He passed away May 9, 1960, at Hearne General Hospital and is 
2 CONC buried at Norwood Cemetery with his Moseley Ancestors nearby.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References''' '''Sources''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Published by Hertzog.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Lancasters from Virginia To Texas" by Mary Nixon Stephens (Rogers) www.txgenwebcounties.org/robertson/biographies/11HOTBM.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Operation Tiger - Exercise Tiger Links 
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exercise_Tiger
2 CONT
2 CONT Served US Army QM Railhead Co, was in Special Forces, was an engineer sent in with a few men sent in with explosives to destroy bridges during WWII.
2 CONT
2 CONT My father was on LST 507 torpedoed by German E-Boat, this is the report kept Top-Secret 50 Years https://www.history.navy.mil/research/library/online-reading-room/title-list-alphabetically/e/operation-tiger.html
2 CONT
