1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)''' was born on February 3, 1893, in Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939849 Henry Edgar Lancaster] and [https://www.geni.com/profil
2 CONC e-34678278768 Mary &quot;Mollie&quot; Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34712167592 James Edgar Stephens]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715940019 Margery Edna Stephens]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715940020 Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717874853 James William Stephens]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34709266998 Ruth Gene Martin]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 9, 1985, in Richmond, Fort Bend County, Texas, United States, and was buried on February 9, 1985, in Austin, Travis, Texas, United States. * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/46307540/julia-eugen
2 CONC ia-stephens#view-photo=189543287 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 20 2020, 23:44:03 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''His Profession''''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was  Chief Dispatcher with South Pacific Rail Road. They lived in Lockhart, Austin, Hearne during his time with employment with the railroad. After retirement, they lived in Marble Falls, Texas until his death, Aug. 10, 1962.
2 CONT
2 CONT Methodist Church Women's Society of Christian Services Local Committee Representative. A very important part of the vote for women to become ministers in the future and to have equal rights. They were backing Women's suffrage[http
2 CONC ://www.umc.org/who-we-are/timeline-of-women-in-methodism] She was very active in many organizations in the Travis and Roberson County area during her lifetime. 
2 CONT
