1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Margery Edna Peel (Stephens)''' was born on November 12, 1915, in Yoakum, DeWitt County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34712167592 James Edgar Stephens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-3
2 CONC 4715857540 Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721278637 Rev. James Carr Peel] on September 10, 1932, in Robertson, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722978530 James Thomas Peel
2 CONC ]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722978621 William Carr Peel]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on September 2, 1996, in Friendswood, Galveston, Texas, USA, Friendswood, Harris, Texas, from Head Injury from fall. And was buried in Texas Methodist Conference Center Cemetery Elkhart, Elkhart, Anderson County, Texas, U
2 CONC SA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Memories of Aunt Margie'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Aunt Margie was the most gracious of the Lancaster women.  Taking the time to listen to everyone and then she would answer concerns in a way you knew she actually listened and cared about you. A gift not many in our family possess
2 CONC ed, we had the gift of talking, not always listening. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the best minister's wife, always cooking casseroles and desserts for the elderly, deceased family members, the ill, students, and whomever in the town needed food. Every time I  visited, she was cooking. 
2 CONT Constantly, church members coming in and out of their home picking up food, or we were delivering food to people. She was never idle and never not smiling and laughing. She always said "a minister and wife works 24-7" I often wond
2 CONC ered if people in the church knew to appreciate their wonderful ministers and their wives. I think many take for granted what they do personally and the time spent. The minister is called by The Lord and his wife follows. My aunt 
2 CONC Margie is to be commended for a fantastic job well accomplished. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember her for many things, but her homemade Divinity and Fudge were the best. She was also a gifted artist, many in the family have her oil paintings.  Also, a musician, played the piano, organ, and led the choir. I miss her 
2 CONC beautiful smiling face. She was warm, kind, and generous. Magnolias remind me of her. her niece, Suzan Martin
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Methodist Church Women's Society of Christian Services Local and District Committee Representative. A very important part of the vote for women to become ministers in the future and to have equal rights. [http://www.umc.org/w
2 CONC ho-we-are/timeline-of-women-in-methodism] She was very active in many organizations in the Roberson and Smith Counties and several other counties during her lifetime. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
