1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens)''' was born on March 2, 1919, in Yoakum, Lavaca, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34712167592 James Edgar Stephens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715857540 
2 CONC Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34728692830 John Cicero Rogers]. Together they had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on April 23, 1987, in Rosenberg, Fort Bend County, Texas, United States. Davis-Greenlawn Cemetery [https://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?indiv=1&dbid=60525&h=51336098&ssrc=pt&tid=111701831&pid=430091807115&usePUB=tr
2 CONC ue]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens) was a gifted musician that could play the piano as soon as she placed her tiny hands on the piano keys at age 3 years, any tune she heard she could play to perfection. Nixey also learned to read music 
2 CONC at an early age, her parents began piano and voice lessons when she showed her gift for music. She was vivacious and lit up a room when she walked in, always making everyone feel special when she spoke to them. She was our Family 
2 CONC organizer, we had family reunions every year she was alive. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She also spent over 50 years carefully documenting and researching our family lineage and we are fortunate she left the paper trail by publishing a detailed genealogy book before her death in 1987.  "Lancaster From Virginia To Tex
2 CONC as" wasn't a storybook, but a detailed paper trail of our lineage. Family Tree- Salt Lake City deemed a creditable source book. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Eastern Star
2 CONT * Daughters of The American Revolution Ntl Number 455884- Supplemental Nathaniel Lancaster[https://www.geni.com/people/Nathaniel-Lancaster-I/6000000009669841225?through=3807239] a direct descendant.  Captain John Field [https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/people/Captain-John-Field-II/6000000038149786515] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References''' [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/50762195/the-hearne-democrat/] Eastern Star, Father was a Mason, as was Grandfather's and maternal and paternal Great-grandfather's
2 CONT https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_descendants/?action=list&MyPrimary_Seqn=479132&MyLineageCount=1
