1 OCCU Chemical Engineer, President of Operations Dow Chemical CO. 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''James William Stephens''' was born on September 21, 1927, in Austin, Travis County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34712167592 James Edgar Stephens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-347158
2 CONC 57540 Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)]. He was a Chemical Engineer, President of Operations Dow Chemical Co. Sao Paulo, Brazil. After graduating from Hearne High School, he enlisted in the United States Marine Corps at the age 
2 CONC of 17. He was a veteran of World War II and the Korean War. In between terms of service he obtained a chemical engineering degree from the University of Texas. Following his service in Korea, Bill enjoyed a long, successful career
2 CONC  with the Dow Chemical Company, focusing on the design, construction and operation of large capital projects in Freeport and Sao Paulo, Brazil, among other sites. Bill was active in many social and service organizations. He was a 
2 CONC long time member of the First United Methodist Church in Lake Jackson and San Marcos. He was an Eagle Scout and served on the Bay Area Council of Boy Scouts for many years. A private pilot since the age of 14, Bill also enjoyed sa
2 CONC iling and motorcycles in his retirement. Until his final years, he was a happy, energetic man who enjoyed spending time with friends and family. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT James William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717875111 Linda Ann Jones (Stephens)] on February 18, 1950, in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, USA. Together they had six children, four surviving.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34747517170 Carol Ann Stephens];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34747517171 Patricia Kay Stephens];
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 6, 2008, in San Marcos, Hays County, Texas, United States and was buried in Lake Jackson, Brazoria County, Texas, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/26706967/james-william-stephens]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Uncle Bill was always on the go, he often called me for last-minute trips on his motorcycle across the USA or to fly. He always stayed in touch, sometimes just to talk, which was wonderful knowing he took time out of his busy sche
2 CONC dule to check-in. I've found out years later, I wasn't the only special one, he called many people and took Liz, his daughter-inlaw on his motorcycle ventures. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He told me as well as my mother, he got his pilot's license when he was a teenager in Hearne, Texas, paid for the lessons from part-time jobs. One day he told my mother and his parents to be outside in their yard at a certain time
2 CONC , he did a flyover, this is how they discovered he was flying. He was ambitious, extremely intelligent, always top of his class in High School and College. He always had a beaming smile on his face and the wonderful warm hugs. He 
2 CONC was one of my favorite uncles who is missed. Suzan Martin
2 CONT
2 CONT * Education: University of Texas, Chemical Engineering, MS.  
2 CONT * US Army Korea
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lancaster From Virginia to Texas, by Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens) Census, Reports "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 195
