1 OCCU Hotel Owner, Bookkeeper
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary &quot;Mollie&quot; Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)''' was born on September 24, 1869 in Bastrop, Bastrop County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278759 Colonel Bingham Trigg] and [https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/profile-34678278443 Frances &quot;Fannie&quot; Russell Trigg (Field)].   
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Behind every successful man is a remarkable woman, such as Mary "Mollie" Lancaster (Trigg). She owned and managed the Lancaster Hotel in Yoakum, Texas. Her husband, Henry, ran a Mercantile and Drug Store; he was a Pharmacist, so h
2 CONC e was busy as well. She was an independent, business-minded woman, and Henry supported her independent nature.  She was a woman before her time; during her lifetime, most women didn't own a business in their own name, and women we
2 CONC re not allowed to vote until after 1920 [https://www.ourdocuments.gov/doc.php?flash=true&doc=63], yet she was able to run a successful business and raise seven beautiful, loving children who adored her. I'm proud to have her as my
2 CONC  great-grandmother. Suzan Martin
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She died on May 6, 1943, in Austin, and was buried in Lockhart Municipal Cemetery,  Caldwell County, Texas beside her husband. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939849 Henry Edgar Lancaster] on November 16, 1886, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939856 Alton Lee Lancaster, Sr]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939857 Pearl Russell Lancaster]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939854 Mollie Edna Spencer]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715857540 Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939853 Carroll Townes Lancaster]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964671 Kathleen Field Lancaster]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939855 John Bingham Lancaster]. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * '''Something Borrowed''' Each daughter of Bingham Trigg received a pair of ornate gold bracelets they wore on each of their wrists on their Wedding Day, each bride in our family has worn the bracelets as "something borrowed" thr
2 CONC oughout our generations.for our Wedding days for generations [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000036572277187?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000103900867065&position=0] 
2 CONT
2 CONT  ''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/?navigation=&perpage=&page=1&sort=_score&search=Lancaster+From+Virginia+to+Texas&fulltext=1&bookmarks=0 Lancasters From Virginia to Texas - Family Search Library]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Obituary[https://www.newspapers.com/clip/34985927/the_hearne_democrat/] Her father, Col. Bingham Trigg Painting is mentioned. The painting was reported as being in Texas State Capitol until the mid-1930s. This painting is mentio
2 CONC ned in Bingham Trigg's daughter's Obituary, one of her oldest daughters of "Mollie" inherited this painting. It was seen by my grandmother, mother, and all of my aunt's. George Bingham was remarkably close to Colonel Bingham Trigg
2 CONC , son of John Anthony Trigg, he visited him often in Texas and painted the portrait as a gift to his niece's husband. I know the story very well, then I found my great-grandmother's obituary with the painting mentioned, also a new
2 CONC spaper article about The State Capital being remodeled and moved to the new buildings in the 1930s. I wish in my lifetime, to see this portrait of Col. Bingham Trigg. Suzan Martin 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Women in America Right to Vote, 1920 [https://www.ourdocuments.gov/doc.php?flash=true&doc=63]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Trigg - Field Genealogy- " Lancaster From Virginia To Texas" by Mary Nixon Rogers, published 1986. attributions attached in photos. [ https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/?navigation=&perpage=&page=1&sort=_score&se
2 CONC arch=Lancaster+From+Virginia+to+Texas&fulltext=1&bookmarks=0] Family Search Library Salt Lake City, Utah
