2 CONT
2 CONT * Hotel Owner 100% in 1907, unusual for women in the early 1900s. she purchased a small Hotel, in Yoakum, Texas, then two years later another Hotel in Winfield, LA After her husband's death she purchased a boarding house. Her favo
2 CONC rite memory was being a "House Mother" for a Fraternity House at The University of Texas", many students attended her funeral years later.
2 CONT * Ownership of Hotels reported in Census reports "Lancaster From Virginia To Texas" by Mary Nixon Rogers
2 CONT *  It was reported in our genealogy my grandfather owned the Hotels, but I found paperwork to the contrary. even Census Reports have her as the only owner
2 CONT *     Residence: 1850 - Jackson county, Jackson, Alabama
2 CONT *     Residence: 1860 - Precinct No 5, Travis, Texas, United States
2 CONT *     Residence: 1900 - ED 28 Justice Precinct 2 (west part), DeWitt, Texas, United States
