1 OCCU Pharmacist, Merchant, Rancher
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Henry Edgar Lancaster''' was born on October 28, 1850, in Jackson Co., Alabama, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964660 John Nathaniel Lancaster] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964663 M
2 CONC ary Ann Lancaster (Jones)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964659 Frances Fannie Lancaster (Lewis)] on December 10, 1878, in Lockhart, TX.She died in childbirth, her husband was distraught after her death, her family took her young children
2 CONC  with them after her funeral, and they continued to live with the uncle and aunt until adulthood. His son, Henry Edgar Lancaster, switched his name to Edgar Henry Lancaster, MD, so he was not a Jr from that point on, he did not ha
2 CONC ve a close relationship with his father. His sister, Frances "Willie" visited and remained in contact with her father stepmother, and siblings.
2 CONT Together they had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964664 Frances William Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743699754 John Alfred Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964669 Henry Edgar Lancaster, I MD];
2 CONT #  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743699755 Francis James Lancaster]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278768 Mary &quot;Mollie&quot; Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)] on November 16, 1886, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939856 Alton Lee Lancaster, Sr];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939857 Pearl Russell Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939854 Mollie Edna Spencer];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715857540 Julia Eugenia Stephens (Lancaster)];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939853 Carroll Townes Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964671 Kathleen Field Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939855 John Bingham Lancaster].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on November 5, 1920, in Laredo, Webb County, Texas, the United States from Heart Failure, and was buried in Lockhart Memorial Cemetery -- Block M. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Profession'''
2 CONT  Prestigious Rancher, Pharmacist, Business Owner. 
2 CONT * Lancaster Pharmacy in Lockhart, and at Manor, Texas for several years 
2 CONT * 1899 he purchased a ranch in Cuero, Texas found Census Records, DeWitt County. 1900 US Census[https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/7602/4118457_00184/70558892?backurl=https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/pe
2 CONC rson/430091807100/facts] By 1930, when the total value of all county livestock was $4.7 million, the number of cattle of all ages reached 58,933, making DeWitt County the ninth-largest cattle-raising county in the state. The Cuero
2 CONC  Livestock Commission Company, sellers of livestock from all over the county, state, and other states, was organized in 1940 and within ten years set several national price records. By 1950 DeWitt County ranked fourth in the state
2 CONC  when it recorded 75,132 cattle. The construction of good roads and highways and the rise of the trucking industry combined to make the shipping of these cattle to market via railroad unnecessary. Rail traffic declined to rail tra
2 CONC ffic and the various shipping pens that had been operating since the late nineteenth century closed[https://tshaonline.org/handbook/online/articles/hcd07]
2 CONT * 1907 his wife purchased a small Hotel, in Yoakum, Texas then two years later purchased another Hotel in Winfield, LA.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- At the time of his death, he owned a ranch in Encinal, Texas cattle ranching near Laredo, Webb County, Texas. He died of a heart attack, not knowing when to slow down, but enjoying what he liked to do in life. [https://www.ne
2 CONC wspapers.com/clip/71310998/obituary-for-h-e-lancaster/]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Behind every successful man is an incredible woman such as Mary "Mollie"  Lancaster (Trigg). The Hotel in ``Yoakum, Texas, was owned by her, she was the manager, bookkeeper and he was the clerk. He owned a drug store and mercantil
2 CONC e business, he was a Pharmacist.  His wife was independent, self-confident, and intelligent he supported her independence, unusual during the early 1900s when women were not allowed to vote until 1920[ [https://www.ourdocuments.go
2 CONC v/doc.php?flash=true&doc=63], 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Education''' 
2 CONT
