1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Edna Spencer''' was born on March 5, 1891, in Travis County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939849 Henry Edgar Lancaster] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278768 Mary Rebecc
2 CONC a Lancaster (Trigg)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939927 Henry Conoly Spencer] on September 15, 1913, in Taylor, Williamson County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-347440
2 CONC 25931 Mary Rebecca Spencer Lemon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 29, 1976, in Southern Pines, Moore, North Carolina, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Aunt Edna was the older sister of my grandmother Julia Lancaster, she lived for a time next to my grandfather "Di- Daddy" and "Nanny" in Granite Shoals, Texas on Lake LBJ. The serene lake back in those days was clear cool water ex
2 CONC cept for the boats going out for fishing or skiing. "Uncle Spence" would take my brother Lee out fishing quite often,  I was considered a bit too young, 8 yrs younger than my brother and too chatty for fishing.   We would dive off
2 CONC  their wharf and swim after they returned. I remember Aunt Edna and Uncle Spence as being both kind,  who took time listening to children. The Bluebonnets and Indian Paint Brush grew all over in the spring, I can still visualize t
2 CONC he splendor. [https://texashillcountry.com/granite-shoals-texas/] Ref 1
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Edna Spencer (Lancaster). Her daughter, Mary Rebecca Lemon (Spencer)  was named for her Grandmother Mary Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg) Nickname was "Mollie"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- '''References''' [https://texashillcountry.com/granite-shoals-texas/] Ref 1
2 CONT * " Lancaster From Virginia To Texas" by Mary Nixon Rogers, published 1986. Attributions attached in photos. 
