1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Rev. James Carr Peel''' was born on May 3, 1910, in Mumford, Robertson, Texas, USA, Mumford, Robertson County, Texas, United States. He was a Methodist Minister with a sense of humor.
2 CONT
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715940019 Margery Edna Peel (Stephens)] on September 10, 1932, in Robertson, Texas, USA. Together they had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 16, 1982, in Tyler, Smith County, Texas, USA, Frankston, Anderson County, Texas, United States from CHF, and was buried in Texas Methodist Conference Center Cemetery, Elkhart, Anderson County, Texas, USA, Pales
2 CONC tine, Anderson County, Texas, United States.  [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/23453317/james-carr-peel Find A Grave Memorial]  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Education'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Southern Methodist University, Perkins School of Theology. 
2 CONT * Wesley Seminary Ordained Minister, Methodist
2 CONT * [https://www.wesleyseminary.edu/admissions/umc-requirements/]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''What I Remember about Uncle Carr'''
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember Uncle Carr with a playful smile on his face, with a pipe in his mouth, one that smelled like cherry tobacco. He could blow different sized smoke rings on command. When he didn’t have a pipe in his mouth, he chewed grape
2 CONC  gum. I seldom saw him in anything other than a suit, wearing cowboy boots before preachers wore cowboy boots. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He seemed to love kids. I say this because he would let us sit in his lap much longer than most uncles, teasing us, entertaining us with smoke rings, or sharing his gum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He loved to tease all people, not just kids. When Aunt Margie said she was 62, he laughed and said, “Yeah, plus tax.” I remember him teasing mom regularly. Mom tended to be a bit nosy about everyone and shared too much of what she
2 CONC  learned. The first and last thing he said to mom each time he saw her, “Ruthie, you been keeping your nose clean?”  Or when he left, he’d say, “Keep your nose clean, Ruthie.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT Uncle Carr had a way of communicating love, beliefs, ideas, information with humor and affection, always keeping the conversations light and usually bringing about periodic laughter. I loved seeing him drive up our driveway.  I lo
2 CONC ved Uncle Carr. Vicki Hester PhD 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children Loved Rev. Carr Peel'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Attending a Church after he left to take his last position in Tyler, Texas, the new minister asked to speak to me to ask me a few things about my uncle. He said everyone loved my uncle Carr, he was difficult to come behind and he 
2 CONC was needing to know a few things that might assist him to settle in. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One thing really puzzled him the most, after services every Sunday his office was full of all of the children from the church. In all of his years in ministry, he never experienced this before. I laughed and told him "Tell them a 
2 CONC joke and give them each a piece of grape gum" Then say a prayer, they leave for the week, happy children and teenagers.  Then the new minister laughed and was relieved to know how to get the children out of his office! My Uncle Ca
2 CONC rr loved people of all ages and took time for everyone that crossed his path in life, he had a special way with his humor and Christianity to touch everyone in his way. He took his job of ministry seriously, but with humor. Suzan 
2 CONC Martin
2 CONT
