1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' James Thomas Peel''' was born on June 16, 1933, in Hearne, Robertson County, Texas USA, Hearne, Robertson County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721278637 Rev. James Carr Peel] and [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/profile-34715940019 Margery Edna Peel (Stephens)]. 
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745074016 Sue Elizabeth Myers] on August 31, 1956, in Harris, Texas, USA. Together they had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Thomas Peel passed gently into the arms of his Lord on May 12, 2021, with his loving wife Sue by his side. He was buried at the Houston National Cemetery, Houston, Texas May 15, 2021. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- '''His Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimmy was born in Hearne, TX on June 16, 1933, to James Carr Peel and Margery Stephens Peel. He was an only child for 17 years before his brother William (Billy) was born. His father's ministry eventually brought the family to Pea
2 CONC rland where Jimmy graduated from Pearland High School and later joined the Army. He served in Germany as a Private Specialist with special clearance at the end of the Korean War. He left with an honorable discharge in 1956. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was introduced to the Meyers family with five beautiful daughters before he was discharged. He was quite taken with the youngest daughter Sue, and she with him.  After his discharge, they were married in August 1956. They recen
2 CONC tly celebrated 64 wonderful years together.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Jim began a successful career in drafting while attending the University of Houston. He eventually moved up in the company, becoming co-owner of Taylor and Hill in Pearland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Sue were the proud parents of two children, Peggy Sue and James Craig, and later he was a devoted "Gramps" to his grandchildren and great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also a true man of God and was a member of The First United Methodist Church of Pearland. He was especially active in his Search Light Sunday School class, providing comfort and care to members and others beyond the class w
2 CONC ho needed support and love. Jimmy's acts of kindness extended way beyond his family and church. He and Sue even volunteered with Meals on Wheels for years.
2 CONT
2 CONT His family, friends, colleagues, and church were his life. Everyone was included in Jimmy's loving circle. He and his wife Sue were the consummate hosts, hosting many family and friend gatherings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally, Jimmy loved hunting. Everyone knew that when the season came around, he was happily on his deer lease. He was up for about any opportunity to hunt for most of his life, sharing his love of hunting, especially deer, with h
2 CONC is children and grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jim is predeceased by his parents James Carr and Margery Peel. He is survived by his loving wife Sue, his brother Billy and sister-in-law Kathy, his two children Peggy and Craig, his grandchildren Kelli Peel Sarmiento and Cassie P
2 CONC eel Yarbrough and husband Mike, his great-grandchildren Byron James, Olivia, Carter, and Chloe, and finally, very special friends Shirley and Carl McFarland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is hard to imagine Jimmy being gone. He was such a large presence in his family and friends' lives. He will be greatly missed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The celebration of Jim's life was on Saturday, May 15, 2021, at First United Methodist Church Pearland, 2314 N. Grand Blvd., Pearland, Texas 77581. Burial was at Houston National Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He loved the book of Ephesians, so we end with a verse:  "I urge you to live a life worthy of the calling you have received. Be completely humble and gentle; be patient, bearing with one another in love."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jimmy" and Sue took care of my sister, me, after the death of our father. He was my first cousin, although, closer to my mother's age.  About 5 and, my sister was 9yrs. old, this filled a gap and brought joy and security in our l
2 CONC ives. Remember his silly songs that would make us laugh, found out he sang the same songs to his children and grandchildren, His grandchildren sang them at his service, and we laughed. Met several people at the service that Sue an
2 CONC d Jim assisted in raising over the years, they're just the rare people that make a difference in so many people's lives that were fortunate enough to cross paths during their time on earth. I always felt special in their presence,
2 CONC  realizing now, I'm but one of the hundreds that crossed his path and felt special. https://www.geni.com/people/Suzan-Martin/6000000062707328387
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His friends said'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 thoughts on “James Thomas Peel”
2 CONT
2 CONT JUDY PARSONMAY 13, 2021 AT 3:51 PM We were honored to have known Jim! We were classmates in the Searchlight Class and "Prayer Warriors" together. Jim showed his love of the Lord. He will be missed. Keep watching for us Jim we are 
2 CONC coming to join you soon. Sue you and the family are in our prayers. Our love Judy and Henry
2 CONT
2 CONT BRENT LANDERSMAY 14, 2021 AT 9:13 AM My heart goes out to Peggy and the entire Peel family on your loss.
2 CONT
2 CONT SUSAN PALMERMAY 14, 2021 AT 10:01 AM I loved my Uncle Jimmy beyond words. He was simply the best! I knew I could turn to him for anything, and he would help me. Men like Jim are few are far between. Sending love to Aunt Sue, Peggy
2 CONC , Craig, Kelli, Cassie, and all of his family during this sad time. Love you all.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID HILLMAY 14, 2021 AT 2:57 PM Jim waS a great partner and a better friend. He will be missed. RIP
2 CONT
2 CONT IAN MACKIEMAY 14, 2021 AT 4:34 PM Sad news reading Jim has passed away, we worked with Jim back in 2000 developing our new technology into the Petro-Chem and refining industry around Houston. He was well respected by all in the in
2 CONC dustry, he knows everyone that mattered in the industry and helped us to get established in the World Oil Capital along the way from our Scottish homeland. Always enjoyed his company when we came over for a business meeting, condo
2 CONC lences to his family he will be missed by many. Ian Mackie Ex Hi-Cad Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT DAVID AND MISSY PARKSMAY 15, 2021 AT 7:09 AM Our prayers, thoughts and love go out for Uncle Jim's entire family and friends. He is going to be truly missed by us all. He had a heart as big as Texas and he always made us smile. Da
2 CONC vid and Missy Parks
2 CONT ----
