1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''John Cicero Jake Rogers, Jr''' was born on June 17, 1912, in Alto, Cherokee, Texas, USA, Alto, Cherokee County, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cicero married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715940020 Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens)] on June 17, 1937, in Hearne, Robertson, Texas, USA, Hearne, Robertson County, TX, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONC  [https://www.geni.com/profile-34728692889 John Stephen Rogers]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34728692624 Mary Jean Rogers]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 6, 1992, in Fort Bend, Texas, USA, Rosenberg, Fort Bend County, TX, United States, and was buried in Rosenberg, Fort Bend County, Texas, United States of America.  Davis Greenlawn Cemetery [https://www.findagrave.
2 CONC com/memorial/86056597]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Jake Rogers put children first when he was Superintendent of Lamar Consolidated ISD, Rosenberg, Texas. He was a dedicated educator, a football coach in his early years, and a school teacher. A good listener with a sparkle in 
2 CONC his eyes. A man of few words, when he spoke it was direct and friendly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1951 UIL  West Columbia, Wharton. Director. General, J. C. Rogers, Jr.,[https://www.uiltexas.org/files/leaguer/leaguer-archives/LE-1951-01.pdf]
2 CONT * 1952 UIL -J. C. Rogers, Jr., Superintendent, West Columbia[https://www.uiltexas.org/files/leaguer/leaguer-archives/LE-1952-01.pdf]
2 CONT * In 1954 - Karate was approved for Lamar ISD - John "Jake" Rogers was a forward-thinking educator and was fair, always thinking of the young people attending his schools and their futures. [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc
2 CONC _id=6000000134612956885&]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Football coach, high school principal before he became the Superintendent of Lamar Consolidated ISD in Rosenberg, Texas until his retirement. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Coaches - '''texashighschoolfootballhistory'''
