1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Jim was a big gentle man who was struck down with scarlet fever as a child which left him deaf and dumb. He married a little scots lady I think her name was Mary and they ran a boarding house in Ashburton where Ji
2 CONC m died from cancer in the early 1960's I believe there was a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hi Maurice, Uncle Jim was lovely, he was deaf and lip-read - I understood it was from maternal rubella?? I could be wrong, relying on my memory from childhood! He used to stay with us in Christchurch and I remember how excited he 
2 CONC was to see some deaf girls signing to each other, as it was forbidden when he was at Sumner School for the Deaf (now Van Asch). He married Adelaide who had been engaged to his brother George (drowned in the Wilberforce River) and 
2 CONC they had a daughter who was also called Adelaide, if I remember correctly! By the way, I edited his name as he was registered as Felix, not James! There doesn't appear to be a second name so where 'Jim' came from, I don't know! Re
2 CONC gards, Cathrine
