1 OCCU Ranchman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT John Phillip Nixon was a successful rancher,  owned two large ranches; one in Yancey and one in Tarpley, Texas located in northern Medina County. He raised cattle and horses. He was one of the early breeders of the  American Quart
2 CONC er Horse, along with his father, Robert Thomas Nixon. With his expertise and enjoyment of ranching, he became a rancher and breeder of Quarter Horses instead of attending college and the medical or legal profession as some of his 
2 CONC brothers chose. He was an early member of The Texas Quarter Horse Association.[https://tqha.com/] Nixon's Quarter Horses are well-known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Phillip Nixon''' was born on January 20, 1857, in Guadalupe County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961279 Captain Robert Thomas Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-126333375 
2 CONC Laura Ann Nixon]. He was a Ranchman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745353008 Dora Ann Nixon (Wilson)] on February 3, 1887, in Tehuacana, Limestone, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745353019 Margaret Nora Nixon];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745353016 Mary Viola Mofield Melton (Nixon)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34690044342 Hallie Laura McAnelly];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745353015 John Phillip Nixon];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745353017 Armour Dora Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34750000363 Mary Renot Nixon ( Neal)] on November 16, 1914, in Hondo, Medina County, Texas, USA.  He died on July 14, 1935, in Medina, Texas, the United States, Medina County, Texas, the 
2 CONC United States from Chronic Bronchitis, and was buried after Yancey, Medina County, Texas, USA. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18006662]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Education:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Philips Exeter Academy - Prep School, Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon was concerned, although his children were intelligent the Texas Schools were inferior to Virginia schools, he decided his children should attend Phillips Exeter Ac
2 CONC ademy as prep for college and medical school. Future generations of our Nixon lineage followed this family tradition through the present day.[https://www.exeter.edu/]
2 CONT * The University of Texas, Austin, Texas
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
