1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Sam Houston Nixon''' was born on January 1, 1868 in Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961279 Captain Robert Thomas Nixon, (CSA)] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-126333375 Laura 
2 CONC Ann Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sam married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819057 Annie Elizabeth Nixon Ballard] on June 24, 1891, in Segiun, Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. Together they had several children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 1900 they were separated and the young children lived with him at his sister, https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stephens/6000000012839840153?through=6000000012839917647, and brother-in-law https://www.geni.com/people/Wil
2 CONC liam-Bell-Stephens/6000000012839917647?through=6000000012839840153 Ranch in Guadalupe County, Texas. He was working with them on their ranch with the ranch hands. His sister and her oldest daughter were helping him with his young 
2 CONC children, ages newborn, 4, 6, and 8. She moved to California shortly after the birth. She moved back, they reconciled and had more children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819061 Eunice Estelle Nixon]; Left with single father 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819060 Margaret Lorena Nixon]; Left with single father
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819064 Mabel Anne Nixon];         Left with single father
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819062 Robert Stanley Nixon]; * Left as a Newborn with father  b 1901
2 CONT 1903 she returned.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819063 John Harrison Nixon]; born 1904 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819065 Nicholas Champion Nixon]; 1910
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819066 Thomas Edison Nixon]; 1911
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819067 Betty Laverne Nixon]; 1917
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34773819068 Mary Louise Nixon]. 1919
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife left for the final time around 1920 for California, and divorce was granted for desertion. He never remarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 20, 1951, in Houston, Harris, Texas, USA, and was buried in Houston, Harris County, Texas, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He chose to be a rancher like his father. He was given the choice to go to college like his older brothers to become a doctor or some other lucrative profession, he loved the land and being out in nature working alongside his fath
2 CONC er, so he took the offer of land and a homestead.  In the first part of his married life, he was a successful rancher alongside his father. He grazed well-bred Durham Beef cattle, a herd of Jerseys, horses, and mules. He, as his f
2 CONC ather Robert Thomas Nixon, was experimenting with crossbreeding of Spanish Ponies and Bay, Spanish Ponies, and Quarter Horse Stallions. He was the owner of a Billy-stock stallion and he continued to have good horses. The Nixon's h
2 CONC orses were used for saddle horses, but just south of their Ranch lived Tom King, who regularly went with his horses to tracts all over the county. "pg 12 "Early Nixon's of Texas" 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death, he didn't do as well. His wife left him with their very young children and a newborn baby.  He moved in with his sister and brother-in-law, to help them with their ranch, and his sister to assist with his
2 CONC  many young children. His wife did return after a couple of years, and they had several more children. He worked as a laborer in a cotton mill until retirement, by 1919 his wife separated, and then they divorced. The Great Depress
2 CONC ion years were difficult for many people.  By 1940 he was living with his son, Thomas Edison Nixon, an Electrical Engineer, and lived with him until his death. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References''' Nixon, Texas founded by his father [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nixon,_Texas]
