1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Judge Edgar Alfred Stevens''' was born on July 15, 1856 in Carroll County, Georgia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717686826 Edward Wilkins Stevens, 2nd Corp, CSA] and [https://www.geni.com/prof
2 CONC ile-34717686867 Mary Edith Stevens]. He was an Attorney and Judge in Rockport, Aransas County, Texas. He published three Law Books. His son joined him in his private practice after graduating from the University of Virginia Law Sc
2 CONC hool, and  passing the Texas Bar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgar married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721312271 Alice Stevens (Benson)]. Together, they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721309118 Judge Frederick Stevens]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 6, 1924 in Rockport, Aransas County, Texas, United States, and was buried in Prairie View Cemetery, Aransas Pass, San Patricio County, Texas, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Both parents perished in 1868, soon after the Civil War. His brother, William Bell Stephens at the age of 12, was sent to Texas to live with an uncle and aunt. Edgar Alfred Stevens was separated from his older brother and was in A
2 CONC labama with a family. He married Alice Stevens (Benson). They did remain in contact with one another. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Frederick Stevens, Atty., Federal Judge.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stephens notes.
2 CONT '''Edgar Alfred Stevens''' was born on July 15, 1856, in Carroll County, Georgia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717686826 Edward Stevens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717686867 Edith Edy St
2 CONC ephens (Kilby)]. He was an Attorney and a CPA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgar married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721312271 Alice Stevens (Benson)]. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721309118 Frederick Stevens]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 6, 1924, in Rockport, Aransas County, Texas, United States, and was buried in Prairie View Cemetery, Aransas Pass, San Patricio County, Texas, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
