2 CONT WILLIS BREWER Willis M. Brewer, 60, of 212 Longfellow Lane, died Wednesday at 9:40 p.m. in a local hospital following a lingering illness. Born July 10, 1918 in Anadarko, Okla., Mr. Brewer was a retired DuPont employee who had liv
2 CONC ed in Victoria for 45 years.  He was a member of First United Methodist Church, Masonic Lodge No. 40 and Scottish Rite Houston Consistory. Funeral services will be Friday at 4 p.m. in the Colonial Funeral Home Chapel, with the Rev
2 CONC . Luster Lockett officiating. Burial will follow in Memorial Park Cemetery under the direction of Victoria Masonic Lodge No. 40 AF & AM. Mr. Brewer is survived by his wife, Mrs. Marie Moore Brewer of Victoria; a daughter, Mary Car
2 CONC ol Greig of Beaumont; and two grandsons. Pallbearers will be Merlyn Goldman, Norm Harris, Herb J. Cole, Del Ray Bommer, David Post and Stanley Baumbach. The Victoria Advocate-Friday, March 30, 1979, page 12A.* Reference: [https://
