1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Frances Russell Trigg''' was born on October 24, 1843, in Culpeper County, Virginia, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964477 Henry Hill Field] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964468 Mary Rus
2 CONC sell Field (Colvin)]. She was a School Teacher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278759 Colonel Bingham Trigg] on September 3, 1868, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, TX, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278768 Mary Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278769 Bingham Trigg, Jr]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278764 Julia Bingham Kleine Cauthorn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278763 Frances Field Coopwood (Trigg)]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278765 Rosa Sue Flowers]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on January 15, 1920,  and was buried in Lockhart Municipal Burial Park, Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39487762]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT They separated, but no record of a divorce, although by her leaving him at the time it may have been considered "Desertion" and he may have filed on those grounds.  On Census Reports she lists herself as married, then after Col. B
2 CONC ingham Trigg's death, lists widow. This may have been out of embarrassment as the stigma of divorce during this era,  for her social class would have had repercussions for her and her daughter.'s.  She raised her four daughters by
2 CONC  herself. She was a woman of means, the daughter of Henry Hill Field, she inherited the land and an estate in Lockhart, Calwell County, Texas where she and her daughter lived after she moved from Austin. She was an independent, so
2 CONC cially active woman in Lockhart until her death in 1920. Her will was probated and her daughters were all named in her will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a District Attorney in Travis County, Texas. She was a schoolteacher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/?navigation=&perpage=&page=1&sort=_score&search=Lancaster+From+Virginia+to+Texas&fulltext=1&bookmarks=0 Lancasters From Virginia to Texas - Family Search Library]
2 CONT
2 CONT Trigg Genealogy ”Lancaster From Virginia to Texas” Mary Nixon Rogers Excerpt From the Biographical Encyclopedia of Texas, pg 217, Barker Lindsay, University of Texas
2 CONT * Trigg - Field Genealogy- " Lancaster From Virginia To Texas" by Mary Nixon Rogers, published 1986. attributions attached in photos. [ https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/?navigation=&perpage=&page=1&sort=_score&se
2 CONC arch=Lancaster+From+Virginia+to+Texas&fulltext=1&bookmarks=0] Family Search Library Salt Lake City, Utah
