2 CONT Note John A. Trigg, Probate Court Records, Saline County, Missouri, Probated 8th day of April 1872. In Record Book B, pg 330, names children: William (married Mary Frances William), Bingham (married Fannie R. Field), John C., ( ma
2 CONC rried Marian W. Finley), Abram, (married Lovie Staples); Mary Rebecca (Marie’s Ephana Wallace), Theodosia Ann ( married JAMES Cooney), and Abner J., unmarried ( last two by second wife, Amanda Harvey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT First Incident - Five years before separation, happened again in 1880- her brothers came to Austin, TX packed her and her daughter, and moved them back to Lockhart, Texas, Texas Rangers were friends of the Field Family, Col. Bingh
2 CONC am Trigg was banned from Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas. [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/34397014/col_bingham_trigg_oct_18_1875/]
2 CONT
