1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [. [ https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/?navigation=&per...] Lancaster From Virginia to Texas - Salt Lake City ]==Biography==
2 CONT '''Colonel Bingham Trigg''' was born on February 26, 1840, in Boonesville, Saline, Missouri, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715937635 John Anthony Trigg] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-347159375
2 CONC 91 Rebecca W. Trigg]. His occupation: District Attorney in Bastrop County, Texas, State Senate Representative for his district, and County District Attorney in Travis County, Texas. Attorney in Missouri and in Texas.  They lived i
2 CONC n Austin, Bastrop, and in Lockhart, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His portrait painted by https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-George-Bingham-USA/6000000080591455968, his first cousin,  hung in the Capital of Texas until a renovation in the 1940s and at that time it was presented to his daughter,  [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278768 Mary &quot;Mollie&quot; Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)] Her oldest daughter inherited the portrait and the family has not traced who has ownership today. George Bingham visited Austin and Bingha
2 CONC m Trigg often.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bingham married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278443 Frances &quot;Fannie&quot; Russell Trigg (Field)] on September 3, 1868, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, TX, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278768 Mary &quot;Mollie&quot; Rebecca Lancaster (Trigg)]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278769 Bingham Trigg, Jr]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278764 Julia Bingham Kleine Cauthorn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278763 Frances Field Coopwood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278765 Rosa Sue Flowers]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 15, 1886, in Manchaca Springs, Travis County, Texas, United States. The obituary leads us that he was buried at Oak Hill Cemetery, Travis County. Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Bingham married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34739822472 Mary A. Trigg] on August 21, 1884, in Manchaca, Travis County, TX, United States. No marriage certificate was found, nor a divorce from the first wife, but Mary A. Trigg (M
2 CONC oore) filed for and was approved for Civil War Widows Benefits. No Issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to Texas following his service in the Civil War in Missouri (1861-1886). The document has an excerpt from the ”Biographical Encyclopedia of Texas with a bio about Bingham Trigg. Assigned is his Obituary, which solves his 
2 CONC death date as May 15, 1886, published in  The Statesman Newspaper, Austin, Texas, May 16, 1886. Cases Argued and Decided in the Supreme Court of the State of Texas, Volume 49, By The Texas Supreme Court.* 
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT After the Civil War, he was shunned by his father for fighting for the Confederacy, he chose to attend McGee College in Missouri, probably for the low cost, he attained his degree of law and passed the bar and began practicing law
2 CONC  in Marshall County, Missouri. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Texas State Library and Archives Commission Copy of original written Petition presented by Col. Bingham Trigg. Had to do with Education and providing equal education as written by The Constitution of The United States and by The S
2 CONC tate of Texas. This was not happening in Texas Schools at this time as it was written in law. [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000036572637973&photo_id=6000000110971621038&position=2][https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000036572637973&photo_id=6000000110971943940&position=1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TRIGG VS STATE OF TEXAS''' Bingham Trigg won his case with the Texas Supreme Court - He was initially charged and convicted in a Texas Court with 1) Official misconduct and 2) being a habitual drunkard. Still, the answer from t
2 CONC he Supreme Court was the proof of four instances the Jury charged him with was not sufficient to establish the charges against him of excessive drinking. No evidence of excessive use of alcohol, day after day, or even every week, 
2 CONC to engender a fixed habit of a drunkard. I believe most important to Bingham Trigg was the Supreme Court found not a single witness to offer or raise suspicion of Trigg, or motive of facts, the charges of Official Misconduct were 
2 CONC reversed -  no evidence of guilt -It was stated unnecessarily to pursue this discussion further. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=AuYaAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA643&lpg=PA643&dq=%22Bingham+Trigg%22&source=bl&ots=nu3f6xaSva&sig=ACfU3U3G2wxmjbU0r-zKznN0E2jsl0-LXA&hl=&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwj81ufJ_rLjAhXMHM0KHSRCCGUQ6AEwBnoECDEQAQ#v=onepage&q=%22
2 CONC Bingham%20Trigg%22&f=false]
2 CONT
2 CONT Incident well-documented behavior after drinking. [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/34307583/the_austin_weekly_statesman/] (reference [https://www.pythias-tx.org/history Knights of Pythias of Texas] The Statesmen Newspaper, Austin,
2 CONC  Texas articles attached. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_Pythias Wikipedia - Knights of Pythias]
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Bingham Trigg defeated https://www.geni.com/people/Gen-Alexander-W-Terrell/6000000024888737406 , Feb 1883 Texas Senate Rep: ("Civil War Soldier, Texas Lawmaker, American Diplomat By Lewis L. Gould" [https://books.google.com/b
2 CONC ooks?id=zRPUAAAAQBAJ&pg=PT88&dq=Colonel+Bingham+Trigg&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjujOrk7rLjAhUCH80KHWuZCtIQ6AEIPDAD#v=onepage&q=Colonel%20Bingham%20Trigg&f=false] [https://books.google.com/books?id=nvxoDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA420&dq=Colonel+Bing
2 CONC ham+Trigg&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjGkeSD4rLjAhWRZ80KHTt2BI0Q6AEIMDAB#v=onepage&q=Colonel%20Bingham%20Trigg&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary, attached in Media] (reference in private practice as attorney represented  https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Ben-Thompson-aka-Shotgun-Ben/6000000021314685958 
2 CONT ''' Ben Thompson: Portrait of a Gunfighter By Thomas C. Bicknell, Chuck Parsons''['https://www.google.com/search?tbm=bks&hl=en&q=Colonel+Bingham+Trigg]]
