3 TEXT Research - Colonel Bingham Trigg- In civilian life Bingham Trigg was a teacher and an Attorney and served as County Attorney of Travis Co., Texas and earlier as District Attorney at Bastrop, Texas. He was born on 26 February 1840 
4 CONC in Booneville, Saline Co., MO. He married Fannie Russell Field XE "Field:FANNIE RUSSELL" , daughter of Henry Hill Field XE "Field:HENRY HILL" and Mary Russell Colvin, XE "Colvin:MARY RUSSELL" on 3 September 1868 at Lockhart, TX. H
4 CONC e died in 1885 in Manchaca, Travis Co., Texas. He was buried near Buda, TX at Live Oak Cemetery on Onion Creek, Travis County Texas. His wife, Frances “Fannie” Russell Trigg (Field), passed away on Jan 5, 1920, in Lockhart Texas a
4 CONC nd is buried in Lockhart Cemetery with the Field Family. Additional research and biography by Carroll Lancaster, Jr. 
4 CONT no proof of divorce from the first wife, unlikely legal marriage to Marilyn Moore by records State of Texas he was legally married to the first wife at the time of his death. 
