4 CONC eft him. Her mother was fortunate to have a family who cared for and protected her in1880 when she left him and moved back to Lockhart, Texas. We were told of this story, now I see it in print. She never divorced him, because in t
4 CONC he 1800s a woman would lose custody of her children, it didn't matter the treatment. As of today, we have not found a Formal Divorce in The State of Texas for Bingham Trigg and Frances "Fannie" Trigg. Any mention of a marriage of 
4 CONC Miss Mary A. Moore was not a legal union, he was still married to his first wife. 
