3 TEXT This was one of two incidences that happened when he came home drunk and was abusive to his family. This time was just 3 months after the death of his young son, Bingham Trigg, Jr and his wife just had a baby, Julia Bingham Trigg 
4 CONC Oct. 7, 1875, Mary "Mollie" Rebecca Trigg was 6yrs old. sad situation. He promised to quit drinking and did for a while, Frances "Fannie" Field Trigg born 1879, until pregnancy with Rosa Sue Trigg, in 1880 . During this time anoth
4 CONC er incident happened while she was pregant, he returned home after a night of drinking and chased her down the street with a butcher knife, the police were called, they contacted her brother in Lockhart, Texas. The brother's of Fr
4 CONC ances Russell Trigg (Field); William Edward Field and Deputy Sheriff Anthony  Francis Field came to Austin packed her and the girls up and moved them back to Lockhart, Texas. Fortunately, The Henry Hill Field Estate left them so s
4 CONC he could be protected and cared for the remainder of her life. She never divorced Bingham Trigg.  The Field's were influential people in Caldwell County, Bingham Trigg did not come near her again. 
