1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Frances Field Coopwood (Trigg)''' was born on June 14, 1879, in Austin, Travis, Texas, USA, Caldwell, Burleson County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278759 Colonel Bingham Trigg] and 
2 CONC [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278443 Frances “Fannie” Russell Trigg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34682926457 Edward Bennett Coopwood] on June 1, 1904, in Caldwell, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34682926460 Frances Min
2 CONC erva Coopwood Morgan]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on September 19, 1958, in Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, USA, Caldwell, Burleson County, Texas, United States, and was buried after September 19, 1958, in Lockhart Municipal Burial Cemetery, Caldwell County, Texas, United Sta
2 CONC tes of America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- I will say, she was a gracious hostess with a home full of guests for her daughter's wedding, very common during the 1920s.[https://www.newspapers.com/clip/38924548/the_austin_american/ Austin American News -Wedding Guest] We
2 CONC  can recognize many of our relatives' names, my great-grandmother, great-uncles, great-aunts, cousins. Today, everyone calls a local hotel and makes arrangements for discounted fees this is the new accepted way. I believe back dur
2 CONC ing the 1920s relatives would've been insulted if relatives chose a hotel.  I know the Coopwoods owned a spacious home, larger than most hotels in the small town of Lockhart, Texas. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Researching my great-aunt, who lived in Lockhart Texas most of her life. I know my great-grandmother visited her often, I found the Newspaper articles of their visits. I wish I had been the one in the family to inherit the letters
2 CONC  they mailed to one another, personal journals. The men were written about extensively in our genealogy books and on the internet I've found quite a bit of biographical information. The woman has been the most difficult because th
2 CONC ey assume so many alias names throughout their lives. 
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-40001/familysearch-family-tree?itemId=745922023&action=showRecord FamilySearch Family Tree] via mother [http://www.geni.com/profile-34678278443 Frances 'Fannie' Russell
2 CONC  Trigg (born Field)] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 22 2015, 12:16:14 UTC''
