1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Henry Conoly Spencer''' was born on January 7, 1892 in Temple, Bell County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744025928 James William Wortham Spencer] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744
2 CONC 025929 Emma Jane Conoly]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715939854 Mollie Edna Spencer] on September 15, 1913 in Williamson County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744025931 Mar
2 CONC y Rebecca Spencer Lemon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on November 23, 1970, in Austin, Travis County, Texas, United States, and was buried in 1970 there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Education'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The University of Texas, Austin, Texas, Math, Sciences, CPA 
2 CONT
2 CONT CPA, Lumber Company Owner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aunt Edna and Uncle Spence were what we called them; I don't understand the Spence unless it was short for Spencer. Aunt Edna was the older sister of my grandmother Julia Lancaster, they lived for a time next to my grandfather "Di
2 CONC - Daddy" and "Nanny" in Granite Shoals, Texas on Lake LBJ. The serene lake back in those days was clear cool water except for the boats going out for fishing or skiing. "Uncle Spence" would take my brother Lee out fishing quite of
2 CONC ten, I was considered a bit too young, 8 years younger than my brother and too chatty for fishing. We would dive off their wharf and swim after they returned. I remember Aunt Edna and Uncle Spence as both kind and gentle, who took
2 CONC  time listening to children. The Bluebonnets and Indian Paint Brush grew all over in the spring, I can still visualize the splendor. [https://texashillcountry.com/granite-shoals-texas/] Ref 1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
