2 CONT
2 CONT '''Military'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Military service''': Oct 29 1942 - Houston, Texas, United States KIA Europe France G Company 409th Infantry Regiment 103rd Infantry Division
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Campaigns:  Ardennes-Alsace, Rhineland, Central Europe Awards: Distinguished Service Cross (United States)-12; Distinguished Service Medal (United States)-1; Silver Star-299; LM-3; SM-14; BSM-2,669; AM-92
2 CONT
2 CONT Commanders: Maj. Gen. Charles C. Haffner, Jr. (November 1942 – January 1945), Maj. Gen. Anthony C. McAuliffe (January–July 1945), Brig. Gen. John N. Robinson (August 1945 to inactivation). Combat chronicle The 103d Infantry Divisi
2 CONC on was ordered into active military service on 15 November 1942 at Camp Claiborne, Louisiana. The officer and enlisted cadre came from the 85th Infantry Division at Camp Shelby, Mississippi, and the enlisted fillers from reception
2 CONC  centers of the 4th, 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th Service Commands (Camp Grant, Illinois, 4,060; Fort Custer, Michigan, 3,845; Fort Leavenworth, Kansas, 1,307; Camp Dodge, Iowa, 1,036; Fort Snelling, Minnesota, 990; Eighth and Ninth Ser
2 CONC vice Command reception centers, 921; Fort Bragg, North Carolina, 600; Fort Oglethorpe, Georgia, 600; Fort McPherson, Georgia, 537; Jefferson Barracks, Missouri, 526; Fort Jackson, South Carolina, 218). After nearly two years of tr
2 CONC aining, the 103rd departed the United States for Europe on 5 October 1944. The division arrived at Marseilles, France, 20 October 1944. It relieved the 3d Division at Chevry on 8 November, arrived at Docelles (Vosges) on 9 Novembe
2 CONC r, and attacked west of St. Dié, '''16 November''', in its drive through the Vosges. Meeting heavy resistance all the way, it crossed the Meurthe River, took St. Dié, 23 November and captured Diefenbach on 29 November and Selestat
2 CONC  on 4 December.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His Death''' at the young age of 20, he died on the battlefield when they attacked west of St. Dié, '''16 November''' his mother received the dreaded telegram no one wanted to receive. . 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
