1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Corinne Pearl Hyman''' was born on October 26, 1875 in Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961279 Captain (CSA), Robert Thomas Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925392 F
2 CONC rances Amanda Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Corinne married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137118 Walter Raleigh Hyman] on November 27, 1897 in Luling, Caldwell, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137120 Aline Nelia Hyman];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742486071 Alta Estelle Hymon];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137122 Walter Walker Hyman];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137123 Benjamin Robert Hyman];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137124 Vance Andrews Hyman];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137119 Harrell Nixon Hyman]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on December 8, 1950, in Luling, Caldwell County, Texas, USA, and was buried in Old Nixon Cemetery, Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- '''The Nixon Women of Texas'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When one views the photo of the spacious plantation home set on 14, 000 acres of the Texas Hill Country, they most likely think, all the Nixon women were the typical southern debutantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attending social events, wearing the latest Paris or New York fashions the Nixon daughters did not disappoint the crowds. They were members of the Junior League, Eastern Star, and many organizations along the way.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon made sure if they desired, they attended the best prep schools, dance, music, foreign language, finishing schools, and colleges as well. This is where the typical debutante story ends.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nixon girls were on horseback herding livestock and mending fences. Many became accomplished equestrians as did their grandchildren. They also learned along with their brothers how to manage a large ranch business.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were able to choose what profession and college degree they wanted, with one exception, their father refused to pay for a teaching degree at a teacher’s college, he said the salary was too low, so they must choose a professio
2 CONC n and a degree they would support them and a family. This was the generation that started our family tradition of the East Coast Prep School, Philip Exeter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nixon daughters and were treated equally to the Nixon sons. This was unusual for this time in history, but normal for the Nixon linage over generations. They were originally from the Friend’s Religion, known as Quaker for seve
2 CONC ral generations until their father arrived in Texas and joined the Methodist Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT After working on the ranch, they would come in in the evening to dress for a formal social affair, their choice if they wanted to attend, looked like a debutante, and being presented to society. If only others at the events would 
2 CONC have seen them hours earlier roping calves and branding cattle, or cooking, cleaning beside the maids, only the Nixon women could do both successfully and with grace.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
