1 NAME Beula Viene Wood (Nixon)
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Luling, Caldwell County, Texas, United States of America
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 SEP 1873
2 PLAC Guadalupe County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 30 SEP 1946
2 PLAC Luling, Caldwell, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The Nixon Women of Texas'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When one views the photo of the spacious plantation home set on 14, 000 acres of the Texas Hill Country, most likely think, all the Nixon women were the typical southern debutantes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attending social events, wearing the latest Paris or New York fashions the Nixon daughters did not disappoint the crowds. They were members of the Junior League, Eastern Star, and many charitable organizations along the way.
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon made sure if they desired, they attended the best prep schools, dance, music, foreign language, finishing schools, and colleges as well. This is where the typical debutante story ends.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nixon girls were on horseback herding livestock and mending fences. Many became accomplished equestrians as did their grandchildren. They also learned alongside their brothers how to manage a large plantation.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were able to choose what profession and college degree they wanted, with one exception, their father refused to pay for a teaching degree at a teacher’s college, he said the salary was too low, so they must choose a professio
2 CONC n and a degree they would support them and a family. This was the generation that started our family tradition of the East Coast Prep School, Philip Exeter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nixon daughters and were treated exactly equal to the Nixon sons. This was unusual for this time in history, but normal for the Nixon linage over generations. They were originally from the Friend’s Religion, known as Quaker fo
2 CONC r several generations until their father arrived in Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT After working on the ranch, they would come in in the evening to dress for a formal social affair, their choice if they wanted to attend, looked like a debutante, and being presented to society. If only others at the events would 
2 CONC have seen them hours earlier roping calves and branding cattle, or cooking, cleaning beside the maids, only the Nixon women could do both successfully and with grace.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Beula Viene Wood''' was born on September 13, 1873, in Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961279 Captain (CSA), Robert Thomas Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925392 F
2 CONC rances Amanda Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beula married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137169 Edmund Franklin Wood] on May 12, 1897, in Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137171 Beula Ash]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137175 Fannie Cheshire]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137172 Margaret Margie Morris]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137173 Laura Wood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137174 Lewis Kent Wood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137176 Julia Wood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137178 Marie Champion Schurig]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137177 Weldon B Wood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137179 Gerald Gene Wood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137180 Merle Wood]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on May 23, 1967, in Luling, Caldwell, Texas, USA, and was buried in Luling City Cemetery, Luling, Caldwell County, Texas, USA. * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/79531844 Find A Grave Memorial] -
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT =
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956- Ref. [2] [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11
