1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Phineas Nixon is not a son of Zachariah Nixon.''' Watch your Zachariah's there were a few of them in the same area, the American Indian's in the area named their children in honor of their Quaker friends
2 CONC  and used the surname Nixon as well over generations. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Zachariah Nixon''' was born on March 7, 1798, in Randolph County, North Carolina, USA, Back Creek, Randolph, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34683064081 Dr. Phineas Nixon, II] and [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/profile-79563906 Millicent Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zachariah married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925391 Sarah Nixon (Thomas)]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961279 Captain Robert Thomas Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928405 Margaret Gaziell Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928407 Stephen Decatur Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928406 John Tinsley Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zachariah married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925897 Gabriella Nixon]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928408 Zelpha Ann Green (Nixon)]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740807668 James King Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928411 Jesse H. Nixon].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1855 in lost at sea on the way to Texas.  Zachariah Nixon's sons that migrated to Texas did leave The Friend's Society Religion by the time they arrived in Texas. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- He died in 1855 in lost at sea on the way to Texas, when he was moving from Randolph, NC  to Texas. His ship and his crew were reported lost in a storm the year of 1855 on their way to Galveston. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/1855_Atlantic_hurricane_season#Timeline] The ship he purchased was to be used by his son, Robert Thomas Nixon, after the move for a shipping export and import business.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Zachariah Nixon''' was born on March 7, 1798, in Randolph County, North Carolina, USA, Back Creek, Randolph, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34683064081 Phineas Nixon, MD] and [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/profile-79563906 Millicent Nixon]. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Wealthy planter in Randolph County North Carolina who didn't believe in slavery, as his many of his Friends Society relatives raised money to send his slaves, his brother's slaves, his uncles slaves and many of The Friend's Societ
2 CONC y Slaves were sent back to Haiti by ship verified by a Newspaper article when his brother, Phineas Nixon, III. Zach opposed slavery, returned slaves to Haiti in 1826, many years before the Civil War,  [https://www.newspapers.com/c
2 CONC lip/36333900/the_arkansas_gazette/] Phineas Nixon, III carried them back to their homeland. The Nixon's, although had slaves listed on Census Reports for generations, didn't believe in slavery, they were protecting the slaves, pay
2 CONC ing them when they worked and were not popular among other landowners around them.
2 CONT ---
2 CONT ---- '''References'''*
2 CONT
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11]
2 CONT
