1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Margaret Gaziell Nixon''' was born on September 30, 1832, in Randolph County, North Carolina, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-79564215 Zachariah Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925391
2 CONC  Sarah Nixon (Thomas)]. College Professor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928431 David Rasberry Bruton] on October 9, 1856, in North Carolina, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928434 Annie Raspberry Bruton]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928435 Sarah Ella Bruton]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928436 Colonel John Fletcher Bruton]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on August 15, 1864, in Thomasville, Davidson County, North Carolina, United States and was buried at Fairgrove Methodist Church Cemetery[ Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/6762995/margaret-gazelle-bruton Fin
2 CONC d A Grave Memorial] ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Her Education: New Garden Boarding School College, in the future, is known as Guilford College. The Friends Society education.  She also attended Bingham Academy. She was a teacher and a college professor. After marriage, she jo
2 CONC ined the Methodist faith, her husband was a Methodist minister at Fairgrove Methodist in Thomasville, Davidson County, NC.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rev. David Bruton and his wife Margaret Bruton (Nixon) were both notable in private education, after graduation from the Bingham Academy, they moved to Wilson in the autumn of 1881 as teachers in the Wilson Graded School[[https:
2 CONC //www.ncpedia.org/biography/bruton-john-fletcher] ].
2 CONT ---
2 CONT * "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11]
2 CONT
