1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''A Quaker in North Carolina to a Prominent Rancher in Texas'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Picture the scene on a street corner in the village of Ashboro, North Carolina when the sun was just rising in the autumn of 1852, you would see the handsome young men mounting their horses, their oldest brother https://www.geni.c
2 CONC om/people/Captain-CSA-Robert-Nixon/6000000075592453259?through=6000000007645907506  age 25 yrs old seated with his new wife, https://www.geni.com/profile-126333375 Laura Ann Nixon (Wood),  at their new covered wagon drawn by a spa
2 CONC n of horses. Robert Thomas Nixon, Stephen Decator Nixon, and https://www.geni.com/people/John-Nixon/6000000077119881878 arrived in Guadalupe County too late for free state land. The first tract of 400 acres cost $800. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Stephen and his wife died, the children continued to live with their Uncle Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon and his 2nd wife after Laura's death,  Aunt Frances Andrews Nixon until they were grown and left for prep-school and college
2 CONC .  Stephen and his wife moved in and began to assist his brother with his children when Laura died earlier in the year from childbirth. They were planning to build a home closer to his brother while Stephen was on a cattle drive d
2 CONC ied unexpectedly in Paris, Texas at the young age of 38. His wife died just three years later at age 34. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Stephen Decatur Nixon''' was born on June 4, 1834, in Randolph County, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-79564215 Zachariah Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925391 Sarah 
2 CONC Nixon (Thomas)]. He was a Prominent Planter and Rancher in Kingsbury, Guadalupe County, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928503 Sarah Caroline Nixon] on July 3, 1860, in Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928506 James A. Nixon]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928509 Stephen Maston Nixon]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928508 Adelaide S. Nixon]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928507 Frances Idella Nixon]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928511 Robert Fulton Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on December 15, 1872, in Paris, Lamar County, Texas, United States, and was buried after December 15, 1872, in Kingsbury, Guadalupe County, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Military Name
