2 CONT
2 CONT Why The Quaker lineage Nixon's may have chosen The Confederate [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_in_the_American_Civil_War] By the 1860s this branch of the Nixon's were not in The Friends Society at this point, they were in the
2 CONC  Methodist Church in Guadalupe County, Texas. Dr. Pat Ireland Nixon, his nephew, made a note in the genealogy book that there were no Quaker Meeting Houses in Guadalupe County Texas, so, this may have been why his father joined th
2 CONC e Methodist church. They were bearing arms and protecting their family, which was against strict Friends Society beliefs. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11] [https:/
2 CONC /newbooksinpolitics.com/political/the-early-nixons-of-texas/]
