1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Nixon (King)''' was born on February 26, 1872, in Georgia, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722417984 William Rufus King] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722418008 Mary T King].  Nurse an
2 CONC d Surgical Assistant with her husband, [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961280 James Wesley Nixon, MD] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961280 James Wesley Nixon, MD] on November 26, 1890, in Wrightsboro, Gonzales, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741435055 James William Nixon, MD]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741435054 Luella Kenley]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741435053 Robert Leroy Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on January 29, 1937, in Gonzales, Gonzales, Texas, USA, Wrightsboro, Gonzales County, Texas, United States and was buried after January 29, 1937,  at The Masonic Cemetery in Gonzales, Texas.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mary Nixon (King) was an extraordinary mother, wife, and person. She assisted her husband as his nurse and surgical assistant.  His medical practice was back in the day when it was horse and buggy days. He was also on call 7 days 
2 CONC a week, 24 hours a day. She drove while he slept in the back, many of his patients were miles away.  He also built a small house behind his home, the first Hospital in Gonzales, TX  to care for critically ill and surgical patients
2 CONC . She was very active in Gonzales Social Society. All of their children were very successful. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''*
2 CONT
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11] [https:/
2 CONC /newbooksinpolitics.com/political/the-early-nixons-of-texas/]
