1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Family and life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/99403385/laura-annie-nixon] ] Obit-Gonzales Inquirer Aug. 30, 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT On the thirtieth day of July, death entered the home of Dr. J. W. Nixon and robbed it of its light and joy, Annie King Nixon, ceased to live in the body. She was born in Webster Co., Ga., Feb. 22, 1869. She united with the Methodi
2 CONC st Church, at fourteen years of age, and came with her mother to Texas the next year: was married Dr. J. W. Nixon, Dec. 29, 1886. No one can say that she was ever wanting to the cause of Christ. She was not a demonstrative Christi
2 CONC an, but in all the relations of life, she proved by her acts of what spirit she was. I never knew a more loving, obedient daughter-her mother's word was her law. After her marriage, she was just as true and loyal to her husband. W
2 CONC hen she became a mother she poured out the purest affection of her young heart upon her baby girl. Young, beautiful, and accomplished, surrounded by every comfort and convenience, loved and cherished by all her friends and relativ
2 CONC es, it does seem hard to realize that Annie is dead. We are trying to be submissive, yet we wonder, why she must leave her little Laura to be reared by other hands, why her widowed mother, who almost idolized her must be so strick
2 CONC en and afflicted, why her devoted husband realized the worth of the treasure he had won. God, alone can tell "why." We feel and know that her sweet life has gone out forever, but that she has only been removed to a brighter, happi
2 CONC er clime. We feel that life is short at best and death is certain and we will soon rejoin her to part no more.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Anne C. Nixon (King)''' was born on February 22, 1869, in Webster County, Georgia, United States of America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Annie married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715961280 James Wesley Nixon, MD] on November 29, 1886, in Gonzales, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742579247 Laura Ann Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on July 30, 1888, in Wrightsboro, Gonzales, Texas, the USA from Complications of Childbirth and was buried Old Nixon Cemetery, [https://billiongraves.com/grave/Annie-King-Nixon/9965214 ]her daughter is buried beside her. 
2 CONC [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/99403385/laura-annie-nixon] 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
