1 OCCU Physcian and Surgeon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Dr. Nicolas Champion''' was a prominent physician and surgeon owned a profitable Mercantile Drug Stores in Luling and San Marcos, Texas. His busy practice was always fully scheduled, his reception room was full.
2 CONC  When anyone walked in on any day they would see happy staff, a friendly doctor and very pleased patients and the family of the patient's cheerfully visiting with one another. He was one of the most popular medical doctors and sur
2 CONC geons in Gonzales County. Dr. Champion's Medical Office was known far and wide in Caldwell and Gonzales County as the town meeting place where everyone was welcome. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After a Houston Post front-page story, he became a bit busier at his practice and drug stores.  In 1898, The Houston Post tried to slur his Heritage. It said, "He was a Spaniard and had received offers of fifty Mexican volunteers.
2 CONC "  His reply was simple and very calmly as "Dr. Champion objects to being called a Spaniard and asks that The Post correct the statement that he is an American Citizen."  Yes, he was an American Citizen, born an American Citizen. 
2 CONC  His patients and neighbors were more upset about the derogatory article, he didn't really care, he just went about his business, just wanted everyone to know he was an American. The community knew him and his parents well. A fine
2 CONC  family. Ref.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Port Isabel, Texas, His father was an Italian immigrant from Italy and his mother from Mexico, but the point was his wife's Nixon family originally being from the Quaker religion didn't care where anyone is from and
2 CONC  consider all Heritages equal. How small-minded The Houston Post was in the 1800s. Enough said.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of Typhoid Fever on July 2, 1902, in Luling, Caldwell County, Texas, United States and was buried in 1902 in Nixon, Gonzales County, Texas, United States. Ref.[2][https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/57013795/nicholas-champ
2 CONC ion]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- '''References'''
