1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Nixon Champion left Texas sometime after 1944 when his daughter was born. He worked in the oil industry in Texas Oil Fields as a Pipe Fitter and continued this work throughout his life in the Saudi Arabia, Dam
2 CONC ascus, Syria and Scotland and finally settling in Louisville, KY. The Nixon family lost contact with John when he moved his family from America to Saudi Arabia, in the genealogy book it stated he was living in that country in 1957
2 CONC  and no other information available. The research found documentation of his marriage, the birth of children, travels, and death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''John Nixon Champion, I''' was born on May 5, 1900, in Luling, Caldwell, Texas, USA. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721943043 Nicholas Champion MD I] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34721942469 Elmira Isabell
2 CONC e Champion]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34749395926 Florence Regina Tribolet]. Together they had two children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34749395935 Judith Ann Champion]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34749395937 John Nixon Champion, Jr]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on April 11, 1987, in Louisville, Jefferson, Kentucky. He was cremated.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
