1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Ann Stevens''' was born in 1832 in Putnam, Bibb County, Georgia, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34746801287 William James Stevens] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34746801300 Mary Stevens (Clark)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died circa 1864 in Greenville, Butler, Alabama, USA Civil War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Story of her death''' We have a Family Bible, but it ends with this era of lineage as well the notes that were taken at the deathbed of a direct Stephens as was told to him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the memory of, William Bell Stephens. He was her nephew, but Mary was raised as his sister.  After the disappearance of his father and Mary's brother; Edward Wilkins Stevens and older brothers, his mother, Edy Stephens (Kilby
2 CONC ) took the younger children to Greenville, Butler County Alabama to stay with relatives. General Sherman was burning the Courthouses, homes and they were not safe in their home in Butler, Bibb County, Georgia. Sadly, soon after ar
2 CONC riving in Greenville Eady and daughter Mary were killed in an attack by the Northern troops. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This left the youngest ones; William Bell, Benjamin Franklin, and Edgar Alfred Stephens to be split up and divided between relatives. They never heard from Benjamin Franklin Stephens again in the future, so we don't know exactly w
2 CONC here he settled in the future.  William Bell Stephens and Edgar Alfred Stephens aka Stevens did remain in contact.  Both settled in Texas by the time they were adults. William Bell Stephens came to Texas with William and Nancy Bro
2 CONC adus at age14yrs to live with an uncle and aunt of his mother's. 
2 CONT ----
