1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Barbara Jean Brewer''' was born on September 2, 1931, in Colorado Springs, El Paso County, Colorado, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717929086 Wilbor Webb Jennings Brewer] and [https://www.geni.com/profile
2 CONC -34760681461 Lena Louise Yazell Weidemann]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34764769761 Joseph Herndon Moring] circa 1951. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34764769763 Edward Alan Moring]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on September 7, 2016, in Kingsville, Kleberg, Texas, USA, and was buried in Early, Brown County, Texas, United States of America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/432205340436 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 22 2020, 3:42:06 UTC''
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/432205340436/facts Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 9 2020, 8:15:15 UTC'' Barbara Jean Brewer Mo
2 CONC ring, 85, passed away on Wednesday, September 7, 2016. She was the devoted wife of Joseph Herndon Moring for 65 years. Barbara was born in Colorado Springs, Colorado, and she was a daughter of the late Wilbur Brewer and Lena Yazel
2 CONC l Weidemann (Elmer). Barbara graduated from Brownwood High School, and she attended Daniel Baker College in Brownwood, Texas. She was a faithful member of the United Methodist Church for over six decades. The family will miss Barb
2 CONC ara's delightful sense of amusement and her spirited laughter. She loved her family, the color green, the smell of gardenias, and ''bling.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband, her daughters, a son, four grandchildren, and five great grandchildren. She is also survived by her sister, Janis. Barbara was predeceased by her son, Edward Alan Moring, and her brother, John Brewer
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service September 9, 2016 at the First United Methodist Church of Bishop, Texas. Graveside service on Saturday, September 10, 2016 in Eastlawn Memorial Park, 1921 Early Blvd, Early, Texas.* Reference: [https://www.findagra
2 CONC ve.com/memorial/169849854/barbara-jean-moring Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 9 2020, 8:23:19 UTC''
