1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Henry Hill Field''' was born on April 6, 1803, in Culpeper County, Virginia, USA, Culpeper, Culpeper County, Virginia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34718939273 Henry Field, of Culpeper County] a
2 CONC nd [https://www.geni.com/profile-34692402028 Frances Field (Hill)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737378 Dianna Field]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737598 Henry Hill Field, Jr.];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737908 Stanton Slaughter Field];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742576418 James Slaughter Field]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964468 Mary Russell Field] on October 7, 1843, in Culpeper, Culpeper, Virginia, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278443 Frances Russell Trigg];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278438 Martha Rosa Steele];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278435 William Edward Field];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278434 Mary Virginia McNeal];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278440 Albert Francis Field]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on January 10, 1858, in Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, USA, Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, United States, and was buried after January 10, 1858, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States of America, Lockhart, Caldwell Cou
2 CONC nty, Texas, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/22695301/henry-hill-field]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He moved with his first wife, Diana Field (Slaughter) to Eufaula, Alabama, until her death, on February 19, 1838. He then moved back to Culpeper County, Virginia for several years. He sold his home in Eufaula he shared with his fi
2 CONC rst wife in 1842, but in the deed, Mr. Field Reserved Ten Square Feet of the lot, which contained the graves of his first wife and child. This became a part of the 
2 CONT Fairview Cemetery Eufaula, Barbour County, Alabama, USA  He moved back with Mary Russell Field (Colvin) and family by 1848, where they lived until 1855 when they moved to Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas
2 CONT .
2 CONT ----
2 CONT William Hill Field was a very prosperous Merchant and large Plantation owner in Texas until his death, his wife oversaw the business with managers until the oldest son, William Edward Field stepped into his merchant business when 
2 CONC he was a teenager and continued to run this business until his retirement.                                                                                 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Field Family land in Lockhart was sold by his widow and children and heirs over many generations. Henry Hill Field left his widow, children, and grandchildren a legacy. Several generations of Field grand-children and great-gra
2 CONC ndchildren grew up in this home that still stands in its original beauty today in Lockhart.
2 CONT
2 CONT The stained glass windows at the Emmanuel Episcopal Church has a plaque in the memory of Field Family name dedicated and donated by the Field family members. [(ref [http://www.eeclockhart.org/history.html F]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Field Genealogy - ”Lancaster From Virginia to Texas” Mary Nixon Rogers Eufaula Alabama Historical Homes Registry.  Culpeper County Records 
2 CONT
2 CONT ‘’’https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lockhart,_Texas’’’ [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eufaula,_Alabama]
2 CONT
2 CONT Field Genealogy referenced he owned 50 slaves, but didn't name them, need probated Will Caldwell,  Texas, around the time of his death, Jan. 10, 1858. A copy may be in ”Lancaster From Virginia to Texas” genealogy book referenced a
2 CONC bove. 
2 CONT
