1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''William Edward Field''' was born on July 11, 1849, in Barbour County, Alabama, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964477 Henry Hill Field] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964468 Mary Russell F
2 CONC ield (Colvin)]. He was a Merchant. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278620 Susan Victorine Field] on June 17, 1879, in Farmington, Sankt Francois County, MO, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278626 Annie Russell Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278635 Sallie Bowen Ritchie (Field)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278628 Margery Virginia Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278632 Willie Lynn Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278631 Edward Clardy Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278624 Susan Victorine Armentrout (Field)]. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- He died on March 25, 1917, and was buried after circa 1917 in Field Family Section in  Lockhart Municipal Burial Park, Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39487711/w-e-field]
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death, his mother and managers ran the business and plantation until Henry's children grew up and returned from college with College Degrees. They did work part-time to assist their mother while they were in sch
2 CONC ool.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Their father, Henry Hill Field left quite a bit of land in Caldwell County for his children and widow. William was the oldest son, he managed it very well for his mother, changing the profitable mercantile business name to "W E Fi
2 CONC eld and Company." from Henry Hill Field and Son's. Over the years the family sold much of the land owned by his father and mother was sold to the city of Lockhart and Caldwell County. Many generations of the Field family lived in 
2 CONC the home until it was sold by William Edward Field's great-grandchildren. The home still stands in Lockhart, Texas in its original beauty. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Education; University of Missouri, MBA
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The stained glass windows at the Emmanuel Episcopal Church has a plaque in the memory of Field Family name dedicated and donated by the Field family members. [(ref [http://www.eeclockhart.org/history.html F]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Resources'''
