1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary A. Trigg''' was born on March 21, 1850, in Clinton, New Jersey, NJ, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34739823175 Dr. William J Moore] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34739823178 Patience Jose
2 CONC phine Moore]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278759 Colonel Bingham Trigg] on August 21, 1884, in Manchaca, Travis County, TX, the USA at her parent's home.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 21, 1937, in Austin, Travis, Texas, USA and was buried at Oakwood Cemetery Austin, Travis County, TX. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Announcement only- Colonel Bingham Trigg married Miss Mary A. Moore Aug. 21, 1884 in Manchaca, TX -ceremony performed by a minister-- but, there is " see facts below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * no Marriage License in any surrounding Counties- nor the State of Texas" No record of Divorce" from Fannie" 
2 CONT * No records in The State of Texas of a Divorce Bingham Trigg vs Frances "Fannie" Field (Trigg)Frances Russell Trigg (Field) wife 1,  was still listing herself as married on Census Reports and as a Widow after his death.
2 CONT * May not have been a legal marriage because in The State of Texas in 1884 a man could not be married to two women at the same time, but Mary A. Moore was approved for Widows Benefits.
2 CONT * No property records found, nor Census Records with Bingham Trigg and Mary A. Trigg (Moore) as a wife, perhaps because he had everything at the time of his death in his law practice name.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bingham Trigg's employment was not in the application for Widow's Pension with the state of Texas as a Travis County District Atty also in Bastrop County, both of these jobs would've revealed the one and only marriage, Orig. Mar
2 CONC riage Certificate filed Calwell County, TX Bingham Trigg, perhaps he never bothered to change his wife's name.
2 CONT
