1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Colonel John C. Trigg''' was born on April 15, 1844 in Marshall, Saline County, Missouri, United States of America, Saline County, Missouri, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715937635 John Anthony
2 CONC  Trigg] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715937591 Rebecca W. Trigg]. He was a Mayor, City Attorney, and Judge.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740800748 Marian W. Trigg (Finley)] on October 15, 1867 in Saline, Missouri, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740800749 Walker B Trigg];
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740800750 Blanche Trigg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on March 20, 1920, in Joplin, Jasper County, Missouri, United States of America, Joplin, Jasper County, Missouri, United States from Cerebral Hemorrhage and was buried after March 20, 1920, in Joplin, Jasper County, Missou
2 CONC ri, United States of America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Occupation: Attorney Private Practice,  City Attorney and Mayor of Joplin Missouri. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Civil War he was on the Confederate side- the reason his father left him a $1 in the Will.  
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.mygenealogyhound.com/missouri-biographies/mo-jasper-county-biographies/john-c-trigg-genealogy-jasper-county-missouri-joplin-mo.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000104230741821&] John Anthony Trigg's son's tied the Estate up for years after his death, they disputed the Will in Trigg vs Trigg. Colonel Bingham Trigg; was a District Attorney in
2 CONC  Texas and another brother; Colonel John C. Trigg; was a Judge in the State of Missouri. Finally, their step-mother settled out of court on August 15, 1880, with an agreement all of the children would receive an equal share of the
2 CONC  land in Saline County, Missouri. The famous transscribed Will is below, but the son's had the last word.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=CeRLZhkWFi8C&pg=PA142&lpg=PA142&dq=John+anthony+trigg,+saline,+Missouri&source=bl&ots=GKmQSEwddA&sig=ACfU3U21ZrI3GHfwK2diZBwhp750CD--6w&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiJi_LEkp3kAhVIF6wKHb5LDJoQ6AEwBXoECDE
