1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Rebecca Wallace''' was born on April 1, 1846, in Saline County, Missouri, USA, Boonville, Cooper County, Missouri, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715937635 Judge John Anthony Trigg] and [ht
2 CONC tps://www.geni.com/profile-34715937591 Rebecca Wyatt Trigg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34820173985 William Ephraim Wallace] on October 22, 1863, in Cooper County, Missouri, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34820173988 Robert T. Wallace];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34820173987 Rebecca Bingham Wallace];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34820173989 Lucy Lucinda Mary Wallace];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34820173990 Lavinia Wallace]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 25, 1878, in Saline, Missouri, USA, Missouri, United States, and was buried after  in Marshall, Saline County, Missouri, United States of America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Excerpt from her father's probated will- Fourthly, to my daughter Mary R Wallace, I give the sum of $400, but her husband has been a rebel against this government, I desire that this small amount shall be invested and so managed t
2 CONC hat my said daughter shall alone receive the benefit of it during their joint lives, and in no event to be subject to the payment of his debts. Fifthly, I give to my daughter-in-law Mary Frances the wife of my son William the sum 
2 CONC of $200, this sum is to be subject to her control and management.
2 CONT Sixthly, as all the children of my first wife inherited from their grandfather Wyatt Bingham a right pretty estate, and which like all other fools they have done all in their power to destroy by the acts of treason and disloyalty 
2 CONC to their Government (the best ever established among men) and for the further reason that my three oldest sons, William, Bingham, and John have been willfully disobedient and unmindful of my best counsel and advice and have sought
2 CONC  and followed the advice and counsel of evil, wicked and traitorously affected persons and they thereby destroyed more than half of my estate, I do therefore and for these reasons, give to said sons William and John each the sum o
2 CONC f $1.00 and to Bingham the sum of 10 cents, which is all I intend for them to have of my estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
