4 CONC m and his brother's contested the Will, it was tied up in court until Aug 15, 1800, when their step-mother settled out of court to settle by sharing the land in Saline County equally between the children. With Abraham's Death Cert
4 CONC ificate, we know he was a Mason, he was in the Masonic Care Center when he passed away.
