1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not to be confused with William Klein ", (April 19, 1926 – September 10, 2022) The Photographer and Filmographer Born in the 1920s in NY" Many biographers have mixed a few films between the two men. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''William Christoph Kleine, II''' was born on August 10, 1902, in Gonzales, Gonzales County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678301349 William Christoph Kleine] and [https://www.geni.com/pro
2 CONC file-34678278764 Julia Bingham Kleine, Cauthorne]. He was a Metro Goldwyn Meyer Studios  Set Director/ Designer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' From a small town in Texas to Hollywood'''
2 CONT In 1925 he left Austin, Texas, and moved to Los Angeles CA. He wanted to further his education after graduating from the University of Texas to work as a draftsman and further his education in film and set design at the University
2 CONC  of California. He had financial assistance from his mother and inheritance from a few family estates he wisely invested in real estate for rental income, early in his career to supplement his salary, His employer by the mid-1930s
2 CONC  was Metro Goldwyn Meyer Studios and pay during that time needed supplementing, By 1940 he owned a home in the Brentwood, Sunset Strip area of Hollywood Hills. He was a successful Studio Film Director and enjoyed his work for over
2 CONC  50 years before retiring and moving with his wife to Oxnard, California. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722670520 Jane Frances Clapp] on November 26, 1945, in Los Angeles, California, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on September 15, 1994 in Oxnard, Ventura, California, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Metro Goldwyn Meyer Studios Film Director/ Set Designer. Over 50 years.
2 CONT '''Education''' 
2 CONT * Undergraduate University of Texas, Austin, 1925 
2 CONT * Graduate University of California at Los Angeles Film and set production. 1930.
2 CONT
