1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Edward Bennett Coopwood''' was born on September 15, 1863, in Camp Co. Tx Pittsburg, Pittsburg, Camp County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744394742 Thomas Benton Coopwood, I] and [https
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/profile-34744394740 Minerva Ruffin Bennett]. He was a District Judge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278763 Frances Field Coopwood (Trigg)] on June 1, 1904, in Caldwell, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34682926460 Franc
2 CONC es Minerva Coopwood Morgan]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 5, 1952, in Austin, Travis County, Texas, United States, and was buried after circa May 5, 1952, in Lockhart Municipal Cemetery, Caldwell County, Texas, United States of America, Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, Un
2 CONC ited States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Judge Caldwell County
2 CONT * Attorney, State of Texas, Private Practice
2 CONT * District Attorney, Caldwell County 
2 CONT * Lockhart National Bank, past President and Board Member.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Edward Bennet Coopwood was a genius in the courtroom, he won many high-profile cases in the State of Texas, such as '''Nixon VS Malone''' - which was for a large sum of money, and involved insurance companies and an estate. 
2 CONC  A widow, [https://www.geni.com/people/Maude-Quinane-Stubbs-Lipscombe/6000000105303706859?through=6000000077119918033 Maude Quinane Nixon (Lipscombe)]was sued by her sister-in-law, they took it to the Texas Supreme Court and won, 
2 CONC he didn't give up when he knew his client's rights. This case changed the lives of her and her son's children's family for generations. He could've walked away or referred her to another attorney, but he knew she needed to win. [h
2 CONC ttps://books.google.com/books?id=Lf82AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA392&dq=Nixon+Vs+Malone+supreme+court&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi2vd7mnLnlAhUJbawKHTYtB2IQ6AEwAHoECAIQAg#v=onepage&q=Nixon%20Vs%20Malone%20supreme%20court&f=fal
2 CONC se Nixon vs Malone- E.B. Coopwood Rep Widow] You can Google and the web is full of Nixon and Malone.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/37895580/judge_edward_b_coopwood/ Judge Edward Coopwood]
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1900 - ED 118 Justice Precinct 1 Lockhart town, Caldwell, Texas, United States
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-40001/familysearch-family-tree?itemId=748368916&action=showRecord FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 10 2016, 2
2 CONC 3:42:37 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT father Thomas Bennett Coopwood, MD  Coopwood House
2 CONT
2 CONT A one-story residence stood on this lot when businessman James G. Blanks (1862-1927) purchased the property in 1896. He added another floor and completed the house in the classical revival style popular at the time. In 1908 Blanks
2 CONC  sold the structure to Dr Thomas Benton Coopwood (1860-1932), a noted Lockhart physician who served as Caldwell County health officer for over 30 years. Members of the Coopwood family occupied the home until 1970. Recorded Texas H
2 CONC istoric Landmark - 1979
2 CONT
2 CONT Location:  In Lockhart '''Refences''' Obituary[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000110635036061& Judge Edward Coopwood Obituary]
