1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Martin Owen Flowers''' was born on September 4, 1874, in Prairie Lea, Caldwell County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744233224 Hardy Marshall Flowers] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-3
2 CONC 4744233230 Elizabeth Johnson]. He was a Judge, and attorney.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278765 Rosa Sue Flowers]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744233252 John Trigg Flowers]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722671584 Eleanor Russell Cabaniss]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on September 12, 1944, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States, and was buried in Lockhart Municipal Burial Park. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT .'''Occupation''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * County Judge
2 CONT *Texas Secretary of  The State 
2 CONT M. O. Flowers	October 1939 – January 1941 during the first term of Texas Governor  https://www.geni.com/people/W-Lee-O-Daniel-Governor-U-S-Senator/6000000020069678111.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Karback-Flowers Home'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Local cotton buyer Julius W. Karbach (1869-1943) had the home the Flower residence constructed in 1911. Built by Louis Neeb, it features characteristics of the Victorian and classical revival styles. In 1924 the house was purchase
2 CONC d by  """Martin Owen Flowers """ (1874-1944), a former Lockhart city attorney. Later elected Caldwell County Judge, he also served one term as Secretary of State (1939-41) during the administration of Governor W. Lee O'Daniel. Rec
2 CONC orded Texas Historic Landmark - 1980 Incise in base: Restored by Mr and Mrs R. L. Hanna, 1978
2 CONT
2 CONT Location:  Lockhart
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''References'''
