1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''John Trigg Flowers''' was born on September 8, 1908, in Texas. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678301366 Martin Owen Flowers] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278765 Rosa Sue Flowers]. His parents changed
2 CONC  his middle name to Trigg, in honor of his great-grandfather John Trigg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on November 1, 1919, in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, USA from Sepsis and was buried in Lockhart Municipal Burial Park, Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT John was an active 13 yr. old boy, who played baseball, ran, and played just like any child his age. Many of us as children had scrapes and cuts, but one of his developed into Sepsis, and within a week he died. He was loved and we
2 CONC ll cared for by his mother, grandmother, and father. I remember hearing this story many times about a young cousin who passed away from a little scrape. Every time we got simple scrapes everyone in our family made a big deal about
2 CONC  cleaning and bandaging us, telling this story each time frightening us as children. Research we find it a true story about our cousin. [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/37724617/john-trigg-flowers-age-13-died-sunday/]
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: 
2 CONT * "Lancaster's From Virginia To Texas" By Mary Nixon Rogers, published 1987
