1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Eleanor Russell Cabiniss (Flowers)''' was born on May 30, 1911, in Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678301366 Judge Martin Owen Flowers, Secretary of The State of Texas] and [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/profile-34678278765 Rosa Sue Trigg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722671728 Weldon Burk Cabaniss, Atty, Sr] on September 15, 1934, in Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34693454445 W Burke Cabaniss];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722671868 John Trigg Cabaniss, Atty];
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722671830 Rosanne Cabaniss]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on August 1, 2002, in Corpus Christi, Nueces, Texas, USA, and was buried in Lockhart, Caldwell County, Texas, United States of America. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''' Eleanor Cabaniss Obituary''''
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor Russell Flowers Cabaniss passed away unexpectedly on August 1, 2002. Born May 30, 1911, in Lockhart, Texas to Martin Owen and Rosa Trigg Flowers, Russell attended Monticello College, the University of Missouri, and the Uni
2 CONC versity of Texas where she was a member of the Kappa Alpha Theta Sorority and received her Bachelor of Arts degree. In 1934, she married Weldon Burk Cabaniss, also from Lockhart, and settled in Houston, Texas where Weldon was heav
2 CONC ily involved in athletic, administrative, and teaching activities at The Rice Institute, his alma mater. In 1947, after a one-year hiatus residing in Key West, Florida, Russell and Weldon moved to Rockport, Texas, and subsequently
2 CONC , in 1964, to a new home in Lamar at Hale Point on St. Charles Bay, a bird-watching paradise where Russell lived until her death. Russell was an avid and accomplished birdwatcher, friend and student of renowned birdwatcher Conger 
2 CONC (Connie) Hager and member of the Audubon Outdoor Club of Corpus Christi. At Hale Point, Russell enjoyed on several occasions visits by families of Whooping Cranes. Russell taught early at Normal School, now Texas Women's Universit
2 CONC y, in Denton, Texas, and later taught English at Aransas County High School. She was a founding member of the EO Chapter of the PEO Sisterhood, a member of Lamar Women's Club, a former member of the Altar Guild of St. Peters Episc
2 CONC opal Church in Rockport, and a member of the Women's Auxiliary of the Aransas County Emergency Medical Services. Russell, predeceased by her husband in 1989, is survived by her children: Weldon Burke Cabaniss, Jr. and his wife, Ch
2 CONC arlotte Cabaniss of San Antonio, Texas; John Trigg Cabaniss and his wife Betty Johnson Cabaniss of Houston, Texas; and Roseanne Cabaniss Fitch and her husband Bob Fitch of Euless, Texas, and 12 grandchildren, 10 great-grandchildre
2 CONC n and one due in August. Memorial Services will be held at 2:00 P.M. on Saturday, August 3, 2002, at St. Peters Episcopal Church in Rockport, Texas. The family will receive visitors following the service in the Fellowship Hall of 
2 CONC St. Peters. Interment will be at the Flowers Family gravesite in the Cemetery of Lockhart, Texas, at 2:00 P.M. on Sunday, August 4, 2002. In lieu of flowers, the family requests that donations be made to your favorite charity. Arr
2 CONC angements entrusted to: Charlie Marshall Funeral Homes & Crematory Rockport-Fulton, Texas 1-800-428-2922
2 CONT
2 CONT Published by Corpus-Christi Caller-Times on Aug. 3, 2002.
2 CONT [https://www.legacy.com/us/obituaries/caller/name/eleanor-cabaniss-obituary?id=39447523]
2 CONT ----
