1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Edith Cecile Lancaster (Ujffy)''' was born on January 12, 1893, in Galveston, Galveston, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745188016 Maurice Sidney Ujffy] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34745188014
2 CONC  Clara Elisabeth Jockusch]. She was a Registered Nurse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edith married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964669 Henry Edgar Lancaster, I MD] on March 24, 1920. Together they had the following children: 
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743968036 Lewis Lancaster]; died as an infant.
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743968035 John Harris Lancaster]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She died on April 28, 1950, in Galveston, Galveston County, Texas, USA and was buried in Glenwood Cemetery in Houston, Harris County, Texas[http://www.glenwoodcemetery.org/]
2 CONT
2 CONT When she died her son was a teenager, her husband committed suicide the year before, leaving John Harris Lancaster an orphan, he lived with the Ujffy Family in Galveston until he began Rice Institute College a year later. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Education'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The University of Texas, Austin, BS. UTMB Galveston-University of Texas Medical Branch, Galveston, Texas Nursing Degree, R.N. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Glenwood Cemetery in Houston is quite an impressive cemetery, notable people of Texas near her and her husband, [https://explorehoustonwithpeggy.com/glenwood-cemetery-houston-spectacular/] Notable People are buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many influential people who have Houston streets and buildings named after them reside in this serene setting.  Daniel Denton Cooley who was responsible for developing the Houston Heights, as well as his famous heart surgeon son D
2 CONC r. Denton Cooley[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denton_Cooley], are buried in Glenwood Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Businessman and well-known aviator Howard Hughes is buried here.  So is Hollywood actress Gene Tierney.
2 CONT
2 CONT William P. Hobby who at one time was the Governor of Texas went on to become the publisher of the Houston Post newspaper.  Those living here in Houston for a time may also remember him as a Channel 2 radio and television executive
2 CONC .  Hobby Airport bears his name. and Glenwood Cemetery [http://www.glenwoodcemetery.org/]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
