1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Lucy Ann Lancaster''' was born on November 8, 1861 in Manor, Travis, Texas, USA, Travis, Falls County, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964660 John Nathaniel Lancaster] and [https://www.
2 CONC geni.com/profile-34852493219 Emily Lancaster]. Adopted and raised by her father and https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Lancaster/6000000075595788039
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34762744448 William Albert Ellison, MD] on September 10, 1894 in Caldwell, Texas, United States. No Children
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on May 9, 1954 in Alice, Jim Wells, Texas, USA, Alice, Jim Wells County, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000075596061039?album_type=photos_of_me&end=&photo_id=6000000205975844821&project_id=&start=&tagged_profiles= Lucy Ann Lancaster as a young lady]
2 CONT Lucy didn't look like the Lancaster nor any of her mother's heritage, it was speculated she was a mix-raced child, of Emily and many in the family thought she was adopted.  She was raised as their own. She didn't have children, ma
2 CONC rried late in life, so we have no one to compare DNA with to verify her heritage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was a '''Documented Slave Owner'''- on June 8, 1840, when his grandfather willed him a precious 4yr old enslaved girl named Emily Hudson Lancaster born in Jackson County, Alabama. She was brought to Lockhart, Texas and 
2 CONC would've became free after the Civil War.[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000223034857902&graph_node_id=profile-34688527390&mode=tagged Grandfather Capt. John Hudson named enslaved 4yr old Emily to John Nathaniel La
2 CONC ncaster ]
2 CONT
2 CONT
