1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Josiah Lancaster''' was born on September 4, 1792, in Cumberland, Cumberland County, Virginia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-2751812 John J. Lancaster] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-2751701 M
2 CONC argaretta Drusilla Lancaster (LeGrand)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722883577 Sarah Lancaster (Ransom)] on October 21, 1815, in Cumberland, Virginia, USA She died soon after, no children born. He joined the Baptist Church before their marriage, her fa
2 CONC mily was members of Sailor Creek Baptist Church, Prince Edward County, VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964803 Lucy Ann Lancaster (Hudson)] in 1823 in Tennessee, USA.  After marrying Lucy Baker(Hudson), he sold his plantation, moved just outside of Bellefonte, Jackson County, Alabama
2 CONC , and purchased a large tract of land. He built a nice home. All is going well for the Lancasters when an untimely death takes him away from his young family. He leaves a wife and two young children. ----Together they had the foll
2 CONC owing children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964811 Ann Drucilla Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964660 John Nathaniel Lancaster]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1829 in Bellefonte, Jackson County, AL, United States.  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References''' 
2 CONT His death
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000188212336829]] Newspaper Notice 1st Notice -
2 CONT
2 CONT March 15, 1829
2 CONT Bellefonte, Jackson County, AL, United States
2 CONT Description:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st notice -
2 CONT Administrator Notice
2 CONT Stating July 21, 1828 was approved a s administrator of the Estate of Josiah Lancaster, when will signed. 1st Notice was March 161829, mentioning he's deceased.
2 CONT Caleb B Hudson, Admin.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd- Final Probate Notice 
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000188211974832]
2 CONT
2 CONT December 20, 1830
2 CONT Bellefonte, Jackson, Alabama, United States
2 CONT Description:
2 CONT
2 CONT Probation of Will, settlement of estate
2 CONT Josiah Lancaster deceased, 1829
2 CONT 2nd Monday Dec city of Bellefonte, Jackson County, Alabama 1830
2 CONT Caleb Baker Hudson Admin
2 CONT
2 CONT wife Lucy Hudson Lancaster
2 CONT Children John Nathaniel Lancaster.
2 CONT Anne Druscilla Lancaster
2 CONT
2 CONT The Courthouse in Bellefonte, Jackson County, Alabama was burned and completely destroyed during the Civil War, all land deeds, and records lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/viewer/273425/?offset=1&return=1#page=1&viewer=picture&o=info&n=0&q= Lancaster, from Virginia to Texas- Owning Institution     FamilySearch Library - by Mary Nixon Rogers] Ref to Family 
2 CONC Bibles, land deeds,  court and probated will docs, 
2 CONT
2 CONT " Lancaster From Virginia to Texas", by Mary Nixon Rogers (Stephens) leads to DAR Patriot https://www.geni.com/people/Nathaniel-Lancaster-I/6000000009669841225
2 CONT * DAR A Patriot of the American Revolution for Virginia. DAR Ancestor # A068352[https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_descendants/?action=findlist&p_id=A068352]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: Josiah Lancaster may have left the Episcopalian religion, when he married Sarah Ransom. It was noted he  is named on a list of members of the First Baptist Mission Society in Prince Edward County, VA, when they met to organ
2 CONC ize at Jamestown, July 19, 1817. He and her family were members of the Sailor Creek Baptist Church in Prince Edward.
2 CONT  When marrying Sarah Ransom, he paid $1.00 to her father. Josiah was a part of many deeds and legal action suits as described on pages 23-39 of Lancaster book of family geneology compiled by Mary Nixon Rogers in 1975.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-262878861-1-159/josiah-lancaster-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-7746d334e9b89799f136ae03645f0d7e&mrid=4c703be94a6d025633e2ec60e58ea384 MyHeritage Fami
2 CONC ly Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 7 2018, 17:18:37 UTC''
