1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT When Ann Drucilla Wildbahn (Lancaster) was born on May 7, 1825, in Madison, Alabama, her father, Josiah, was 32, and her mother, Lucy, was 21. Her father passed away in circa 1834 and after her mother married Judge Thompson Mason 
2 CONC Rector, they also migrated to Manor, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Isaac Wildbahn in 1850 in Bellefonte, Jackson, Alabama. He was a successful plantation and merchant owner in Alabama and Texas. They had six children during their marriage, only three lived to adulthood. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Windbahn Plantation was a working ranch and farm with several thousand acres. Isaac Wildbahn bred horses and cattle as well as successful mercantile stores in Travis County, Texas. He fought for The Texas Calvary during the Civil 
2 CONC War and died on August 25, 1866, at age 51 yrs old and just three years after their move,  when they were finally getting settled, The fencing was finished, their large home was built, five children born, but  one died as an infan
2 CONC t and two lost to illness.  Now Ann Drucilla faces another loss her beloved husband. She never does not marry again, he left her financially secure and she was independently minded and was able to manage quite well.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A Telegram reached San Saba''', on the tenth of February, bringing the sad intelligence of the death of Mrs. A.D. Wildbahn, which took place at Austin on the morning of that day.
2 CONT Mrs. Wildbahn has for the past few years spent a part of each year with her daughter Mrs. J.H. Martin of this place where she has formed a large circle of friends, who had learned to appreciate and admire her strength of mind and 
2 CONC character, her broad Christian sympathies and her quiet unobtrusive benevolence. Her life was in the highest and noblest sense a success. The untiring energy, the pure and lofty motives, and the sweet charities which characterize 
2 CONC and consecrated it, have left their undying influence upon those who come after her.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fullness of years and with her life's labors complete, she has gone from these scenes of toil and pain and sorrow, to where she can feel their sting no more. But to those she has left behind; to those whose youth has been g
2 CONC uided and served by her inspiring influence and example; to those whose burdens have been lightened by her thoughtful care and solicitude; to those whose pilgrimage has been brightened by her sympathetic companionship; to those wh
2 CONC ose lives have been lighted and strengthened by her pure and exalted character; to all these there has come a blank; the painful shock of separation; The Chilling scene of an irreparable loss. But they mourn not as those who have 
2 CONC no hope; the pain of separation is soothed by sacred and consoling memories of the departed, and faith points to a happy reunion beyond the skies, where the holy links of affection that have been sundered here will be reunited.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Friend. San Saba County News (San Saba, Texas) Friday, February 26, 1892* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/81971851/ann-drucilla-wildbahn Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 Sma
2 CONC rtCopy]:
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ann Drucilla Wildbahn''' was born on May 7, 1825, in Madison County, Alabama, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964807 Josiah Lancaster] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964803 Lucy Ann La
2 CONC ncaster (Hudson)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578807 Isaac Wildbahn]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578852 Katherine Rector Townes]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578874 Anne Parsons Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578883 Frank Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578917 Lucy H Martin]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578955 John Edgar Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578891 Ernest Wildbahn]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 10, 1892, in Manor, Travis Co., TX and was buried in the Rector Family Section of the Manor Cemetery, Manor, Travis County, TX. 
2 CONT ----
