1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Rebecca Louise Carrington''' was born on December 7, 1946, in Travis County, Texas, United States of America. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743704609 Victor Metz Carrington] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-
2 CONC 34743704548 Patricia Smith (Giles)].  Research Physicist at the Stanford University Research Facility at Los Alamos National Laboratory [https://www.lanl.gov/science-innovation/science-facilities/index.php].
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Rebecca Carrington''' was a  brilliant Research Physicist with The Stanford Research Facility, Los Alamos of the University, with a bright future when she passed away at the age of 32. She received her MS in Physics from Stanf
2 CONC ord University in 1976 after her undergraduate degree from Southern Methodist University. She just finished her thesis for her doctorate with Stanford University while working at Los Almos. She became very ill again with cancer, a
2 CONC fter previous breast cancer and surgery she was clear of cancer and returned with the Research Group at Los Almos. She called her husband to come to pick her up, she came home, died on Sunday, April 15, 1979.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Each year Stanford University chooses a student to receive the '''Prestigious Rebecca Carrington Award for excellence in research and teaching excellence in research and teaching''', this has been awarded each year since her death
2 CONC  in 1979.  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Education;
2 CONT * Stanford University, California, Doctorate Physics 
2 CONT * Southern Methodist University 1967, Masters Physics 
2 CONT * Phi Beta Cappa
2 CONT * Chi Omega 
2 CONT * Kappa Mu Epsilon
2 CONT * Lamda Delta
2 CONT * Angel Flight
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Personal Life''' Rebecca married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743704841 Theodore R Howell] on May 20, 1967, in Dallas, Dallas County, TX, United States.  Rebecca married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743704840 James N Ecks
2 CONC tein, PhD] on July 22, 1978, in Santa Clara, California, USA.  She died on April 15, 1979, after a brave fight from Breast Cancer in Santa Clara County, California, United States of America and was buried after April 15, 1979, in 
2 CONC Austin, Travis County, Texas, United States of America. 
2 CONT ----
