1 OCCU Elementary School Teacher
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her husband of 48 years, Richard “Dick” Curry Giles, Sr., during college, and gave birth to their four children over the next five years. She later returned to college and completed her bachelor’s and master’s degrees 
2 CONC in education at the University of Houston. Saralu poured creativity, energy, and love into teaching elementary school-aged children for over 35 years in San Antonio, Houston, and Dallas public schools, and as an educational diagno
2 CONC stician for several years in Houston. She was an ardent advocate for her students and held high standards for them. Those who made honor roll were treated to a ride in her spiffy red convertible. Many students returned to see her 
2 CONC and thank her years after she taught them. She was named “Outstanding Teacher” at Ben Milam Elementary School. She was a member and youth group leader at First Christian Church when she lived in Houston'''Saralu Couch''' was born 
2 CONC on November 20, 1934, in Aransas Pass, Aransas County, Texas, United States of America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Saralu married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743704549 Richard Curry Giles, Jr.] on February 15, 1956, in Austin, Travis County, TX, United States. Together they had three children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744052801 Hollyce Chareen Giles]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744052802 Catherine Lynn Giles-Miller]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744052803 Frank William Giles]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on July 21, 2017, in Grapevine, Tarrant County, Texas, United States of America, and was buried at Bluebonnet Hills Memorial Park Cemetery in Colleyville, Tarrant County, Texas, United States of America. 
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Education'''
2 CONT * Southern Methodist University - attended until 1956
2 CONT * The University of Houston, Graduate. bachelor’s and master’s degrees in education 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''References''
2 CONT
2 CONT * "Lancaster From Virginia to Texas" by Mary Nixon Rogers, published 1987 Giles Genealogy H-32 , pg 101
2 CONT * Find-a-grave[https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/181707150]
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/432134237409 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 19 2019, 16:06:03 UTC''
2 CONT ** Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/432134237409/facts Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 19 2019, 17:31:40 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Saralu Couch Giles, 82, of Grapevine, passed away on July 21, 2017. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A graveside service will be held at 10:00 A.M. Monday, July 31st at Bluebonnet Hills Memorial Park in Colleyville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Aransas Pass, Texas on November 20, 1934.
2 CONT
2 CONT She graduated from Aransas Pass High School, and attended Southern Methodist University, and the University of Texas at Austin, majoring in fashion design and merchandising. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her husband of 48 years, Richard “Dick” Curry Giles, Sr., during college, and gave birth to their four children over the next five years. She later returned to college and completed her bachelor’s and master’s degrees 
2 CONC in education at the University of Houston. Saralu poured creativity, energy, and love into teaching elementary school-aged children for over 35 years in San Antonio, Houston, and Dallas public schools, and as an educational diagno
2 CONC stician for several years in Houston. She was an ardent advocate for her students, and held high standards for them. Those who made honor roll were treated to a ride in her spiffy red convertible. Many students returned to see her
2 CONC  and thank her years after she taught them. She was named “Outstanding Teacher” at Ben Milam Elementary School. She was a member and youth group leader at First Christian Church when she lived in Houston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saralu spoiled her grandchildren and her dogs, most recently, her Shih Tzu, Peppy. She loved gardenias, sewing, quilting, Mario Lanza, baking, and cooking special meals for her family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Saralu was preceded in death by her husband, Richard Curry Giles, Sr., and her parents, William Cecil “Kokie” and Helen Couch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: Saralu is survived by daughter, Hollyce “Sherry” Giles and her husband, Glenn Hudak of Greensboro, North Carolina; son, Richard Curry Giles, Jr., of Hutto, Texas; daughter, Catherine “Kerry” Lynn Giles-Miller and her hu
2 CONC sband, Bill Miller of Arlington; and Frank William Giles of Grand Prairie; brother and sister-in law, William Lynn and Bobbie Couch, of Dallas, grandchildren, William Giles Tesdell, Nicole Hudak Linney and husband Jake Linney, Ben
2 CONC  Hudak, Joshua Miller, Grace Miller, Sarah Miller, great grandchildren, Bella Linney, and Jay Linney, and several nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Saralu’s family would like to thank the many people who supported and cared for her, most especially her cherished neighbors, the Ihrigs, Judyckis, and Clutterbucks, and her devoted caregiver, Joy Murphy.
2 CONT
2 CONT BLUEBONNET HILLS FUNERAL HOME
