2 CONC : ''Feb 7 2018, 14:13:58 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Notes''': Margaret was born on February 13, 1929 and passed away on Wednesday, June 27, 2012.<BR />Margaret was a resident of Houston, Texas.<BR />Service InformationMemorial Service Saturday, June 30, 2012 2:00pm - 3:00pm Ch
2 CONC rist Church Presbyterian 106 S 3Rd St Bellaire, TX 77401-4447 713-667-6574<BR />Driving Directions.<BR />
2 CONT ** Reference: [http://www.tributes.com/show/Margaret-Lancaster-94039192 Tributes.com] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 7 2018, 14:16:01 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT MARGARET LANCASTER OBITUARYMargaret "Peggy" Lancaster ,83, of Houston, Texas passed away June 27, 2012 after a courageous battle against cancer. Peggy was born February 13, 1929 in Brownsville, Texas. In 1950, she married Charles 
2 CONC Lancaster. After raising four children, she earned a master's degree in education from U of H. One of her true joys was teaching special education at Sutton Elementary in the Houston Independent School District. She was a devoted 
2 CONC Christian and active member of Christchurch Presbyterian. She enjoyed reading good books and playing bridge with friends. Most of all, she treasured time with her family. Peggy is survived by her sister, Kyle Buske of Wisconsin; f
2 CONC our children and their spouses, Tom and Gail Lancaster of Katy, Texas, Ted and Melodie Lancaster of Katy, Texas, Tim Lancater of Fort Worth, Texas, Kyle and Paul Swetlick of Marquez, Texas; four grandchildren and seven great-grand
2 CONC children. She is preceded in death be her husband of 58 years, Charles Lancaster. A Memorial Service will be held at 2pm, Saturday, June 30th at Christchurch Presbyterian: 5001 Bellaire Blvd., Bellaire, Texas 77401.
2 CONT Published by Houston Chronicle on Jul. 1, 2012.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/275868638/margaret_elizabeth-lancaster Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 29 2
