1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dorothy was born out of wedlock in 1911 her mother died when she was about 5 she then went to live with her father or his family. Her memories were of a big house with servants and boarding schools near epping fore
2 CONC st going to church and Barclays Bank. In 1925 she was put on a boat called the Athenic in Southport and exported to Port Chalmers New Zealand to live with strangers called Jeffs in Otaraia and was married to their brother Charles 
2 CONC who was 22years her senior and they moved to Tinwald. The marriage lasted about 5yrs and there was 1 child named Robert it was in Tinwald that she met Joseph Good with whom she had 4 children and died in Nelson in 1969 after a lon
2 CONC g illness. In 1925 the new zealand government ran a scheme where they paid the fares of young people from Britain to come to live in NZ in an effort to populate the land and be a source of labour  which is what most of themwere. O
2 CONC n arrival they were fostered out to families. . What a suckey story. Real proud of you grandfather john. you sound like a real humane being [not a spelling mistake.]
