2 CONT == Biography ==Sarah, daughter of Buckner Kimball and his wife Pattie Harris, was born 2 January 1773 at Anson County, North Carolina. 
2 CONT She married Penuel Wood (born 22 January 1772, Randolph County, North Carolina). Their son William Wood was born 8 January 1796. Penuel died 8 January 1841; Sarah also died in 1841. &lt;ref&gt;
2 CONT [InternetShortcut]URL=https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~westharris/genealogy/WestHarrisDescendants.htm#c1076&lt;/ref&gt;
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research note==
2 CONT Burrell (4) Wood, b April 4, 1770, d May 1, 1847 md. Margaret 
2 CONT Burkhead and lived in Davidson Co. NC where he died without issue.  
2 CONT His nephew, Gray Wood lived with him and inherited his property.IV Penuel (4) Wood, b Jan 22, 1772, d Jan 8, 1841. md. (1) Miss Smithson 
2 CONT and (2) Sarah Kimball.  According to Mrs. Burchard, who is a 
2 CONT descendant of the second marriage, Sarah Kimball was the daughter of 
2 CONT Buckner Kimball (b 1746, d 1812 in Granville Co. NC), who was a 
2 CONT Captain in the Revolution.  Buckner Kimball was the son of Peter  Kimball and Winnie Gilliam and the grandson of Joseph Kimball &lt;ref&gt;http://files.usgwarchives.net/special/afas/unpublished/Virginia/vol1/unpubva01.txt&lt;/ref&
2 CONC gt;
2 CONT They both died in Randolph County. &lt;ref&gt;[http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_descendants/?action=list&amp;MyPrimary_Seqn=1252685&amp;MyLineageCount=1 DAR descendant record], patriot ancestor West Harris, Sr.:
