1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Morgan Gilbert Denman''' was born in 1792 in Wilkes County, Georgia, USA. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-104184089 Christopher Denman] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-77439922 Nancy Denman]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgan Gilbert married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743835928 Edith Denman] in 1852. no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgan Gilbert married [https://www.geni.com/profile-126333366 Henrietta Denman] on May 5, 1854, in Guadalupe County, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-111705987 Judge Leroy Gilbert Denman] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgan Gilbert married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34642596773 Elizabeth H. Denman (Gray)]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-117040676 Benoni Gilbert Denman, MD]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-117040729 Moses Richard Denman, MD]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-116928875 Morgan Gilbert Denman, Jr.]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 24, 1873, in Guadalupe, TX, United States and was buried after February 25, 1873, at The Old Nixon Cemetery by his wife, Henriette Denman (Andrews). 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He moved from Georgia to Leake County area Mississippi for the fertile land to grow his crops. He was very prosperous and his first wife, Elizabeth H. Denman (Gray)  they have three healthy children all was going very well until h
2 CONC er death in circa 1849, He then married  a widow, Edith Denman about 1852, then they decided to sell the land in Mississippi and move to Texas along with other families members.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They purchased a nice piece of land in Guadalupe County, Texas, bought stock, horses, and started farming and raising horses. He owned a Mechantile store also. The business was doing well, but the Civil Wr was stirring up.  Then E
2 CONC dith became ill and died on March 11, 1854. Morgan Denman married for the last time to widow Henrietta Wood (Andrews), mother-in-law to his long-time friend Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon, her daughter Laura Ann Nixon (Wood). This marr
2 CONC iage was a long and happy one, it produced a son [https://www.geni.com/profile-111705987 Judge Leroy Gilbert Denman]  who would grow up to be a prestigious Judge with the Supreme Court Justice in Texas and many more accomplishment
2 CONC s. Another Texas Nixon Sucess from hard work, determination, well and high intellect.  ---,
2 CONT * Reference: "Denman Family History From the Earliest Authentic  Records down to Present Day" by Harris, Harriet Newell [https://archive.org/details/denmanfamilyhis00harrgoog/page/n16]
2 CONT *"Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89082553272&view=1up&seq=11 Hathitru
2 CONC st]
2 CONT ----
