2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Martha Harris''' was born in 1790 in Granville County, North Carolina, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34760210819 Newsom Harris] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34760210844 Mary &quot;Polly&quot; Harris].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722035065 Richard Andrews]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725123815 Christena Winslow];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34723310199 Elizabeth Lyndon (Andrews)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-126333366 Henrietta Denman];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725123814 Roland Harris Andrews];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34763253234 Wiley W. Andrews];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34723310343 Lenida Lunday Thornburgh];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725123818 Wiley W. Andrews]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after August 14, 1860, in Granville, North Carolina, United States, and was buried after  in New Hope Methodist Church, Randolph County, North Carolina, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 260-263. In the Madison County, Tenn. County Court, Sept. 8, 1858, it was revealed that on Feb. 6, 1855, the clerk and master had sold land and negroes to JESSE W. WINSTON, 121 acres and as he had paid for this completely the cour
2 CONC t vested title to this acreage to him and divested from''' ISHAM V. HARRIS''', Texas; THOMAS H. HARRIS, Illinois; LEVIN M. HARRIS, Texas; STEPHEN R.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Page 13)
2 CONT
2 CONT HARRIS, Texas;''' WILEY T. HARRIS,''' Madison Co., Tenn. ; PRESSER LEWELLEN, widow of JOHN LEWELLEN, Henderson Co., Tenn.;''' MARTHA ANDREWS, widow of RICHARD ANDREWS''', North Carolina; NANCY FULLER and husband, ALLEN FULLER, Ill
2 CONC inois — assigned to J. F. Clark who also appeared for himself; ELIZABETH RAWLINGS, Madison Co., Tenn., wife of AUGUSTUS RAWLINGS and only child of DUKE H. HARRIS; NOAH A. NICHOLS and ANDERSON T. NICHOLS, Texas, only children of SA
2 CONC RAH NICHOLS, dec. who was a daughter of WILEY T. HARRIS; the children of DOVE C. ROGERS, dec. who was a daughter of WILEY T. HARRIS (their names: GIDEON B. ROGERS, Missouri; JAMES ROGERS, California; JACOB ROGERS, Ark. by his next
2 CONC  friend, Rolin A. Anderson; WINEFORD DOVE McNEAL, child of JOHN and ELIZABETH McNEAL, the latter of whom was a daughter of Dove C. Rogers and is now deceased, and Wineford Dove McNeal was represented by JOHN McNEAL, Kentucky); the
2 CONC  children of JAMES HARRIS who died about 1838 (names: CHESTAIN HARRIS, THOMAS J. HARRIS, JAMES HARRIS, Illinois, the latter represented by A. T. Johnson); RUFUS D. JOHNSON, only child of MIRANDA G. JOHNSON who died about 1838 and 
2 CONC Rufus was a minor represented by his father, ALEXANDER. JOHNSON, Decatur Co., Tenn.; the children of WILLIAM HARRIS, now dec (LOVE D. HARRIS, Madison Co., Tenn.; GEORGE M. HARRIS, Texas; ARTHUR D. HARRIS, Madison Co., Tenn., a min
2 CONC or represented by Love D. Harris; ADELIA WEST of Ark., widow of PHILLIP T. WEST; JEROME B. WEST and husband, JAMES WEST, Fayette Co., Tenn.; MARY ADAMS and husband, JAMES ADAMS, Madison Co., Tenn.; JANE L. HARRIS, represented by h
2 CONC er mother, NANCY HARRIS; NANCY M. HARRIS, represented by her mother, NANCY HARRIS; the children of THYRES CHAMBERLAIN who was a daughter of WILLIAM HARRIS and the dec wife of CHARLES CHAMBERLAIN, Shelby Co., Tenn. (names: GEORGE W
2 CONC . CHAMBERLAIN, JAMES EDWARD CHAMBERLAIN, represented by their father, CHARLES CHAMBERLAIN; the four children of NARCISSA D. ALEXANDER, dec wife of JAMES M. ALEXANDER, Missouri, she having been a daughter of WILLIAM HARRIS (names: 
2 CONC LOUISA JANE ALEXANDER, SARAH AMANDA ALEXANDER, MARY MERANDA ALEXANDER, FELIX DUNCAN ALEXANDER, minors represented by NANCY HARRIS, Madison Co., Tenn.). Reg March 25, 1859.
2 CONT
