1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Patrick Ireland Nixon Jr, MD''' was born on May 28, 1913, in San Antonio, Bexar County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34687119548 Patrick Ireland Nixon, I, MD] and [https://www.geni.com/pr
2 CONC ofile-34687119550 Olive Gray Nixon (Read)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328374 Ruby Leona Baker] on March 6, 1942, in New York, West Point. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328376 Pat Ireland Nixon, III]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328377 Margaret Frances Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328378 John Baker Nixon Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328379 Nancy Lee LaBounty]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742328373 Della Mae Torres] on May 6, 1983, in Bexar, Texas, USA.  He died at the age of 99 on October 20, 2012, in San Antonio, Bexar, Texas, USA, and was buried after October 20, 2
2 CONC 012, in San Antonio, Bexar County, Texas, United States of America,
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Jr. graduated from the University of Texas at Austin in 1935 and Duke University Medical School in 1939. In 1949 he joined the Army and was stationed at West Point during WWII as a Hygiene Teacher and was a 
2 CONC member of the Medical Staff. In 1946 he returned to practice medicine with father in San Antonio. After his first wife, Ruby passed away in 1982, he married for a second time to Della. He enjoyed his hobby of collecting old antiqu
2 CONC e cars and donating much of his time to charity and working for the Boy Scouts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
