1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Edmund Franklin Wood married Buela Vienne Wood (Nixon) her dowry was a large parcel of ranch land. which they both worked very well.  He was a remarkably successful rancher, but it was a sad time for them, Cap
2 CONC tain Robert Thomas Nixon died just two months before their wedding. it was the first stage of change for the childhood plantation she grew up on, but Ed Wood build a lovely home for his family and was a wonderful husband, father, 
2 CONC and grandfather. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert T. Nixon founded the original settlement of Nixon, Guadalupe, County, now known as the ghost town "Old Nixon;" a former 14,000-acre plantation between Belmont-Luling, Guadalupe, County. Running cattle and horse-breeding was
2 CONC  the focus of the Nixon Plantation, by 1899 they had a cotton gin, Nixon family-owned, two schools, "Wagners Store' Nixon's and Stephens; Dealers in Dry Goods, Notions, Fine Groceries and General Merchandise, Owned by William Bell
2 CONC  Stephens and Sam Nixon. The only remaining establishment of the original Old Nixon is its Cemetery. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Edmund Franklin Wood''' was born on February 12, 1867, in Montgomery County, North Carolina, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740807672 Beula Viene Wood] on May 12, 1897 in Guadalupe County, Texas, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137171 Beula Ash];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137175 Fannie Cheshire];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137172 Margaret Margie Morris];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137173 Laura Wood];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137174 Lewis Kent Wood];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137176 Julia Wood];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137178 Marie Champion Schurig];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137177 Weldon B Wood];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137179 Gerald Gene Wood];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34741137180 Merle Wood]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on September 30, 1946, in Luling, Caldwell, Texas, USA from  Coronary Thrombosis and was buried after in Luling City Cemetery, Luling, Caldwell County, Texas, USA. * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/79531821
2 CONC /edmund-franklin-wood Find A Grave Memorial] 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
