1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/432122668254 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 24 2019, 6:43:21 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gene Wood, Father, rancher, oilman, U.S. Army veteran and "all around good guy" went to his eternal rest at the age of 95 on April 9, 2011. Gene was born to Edmund Franklin Wood and Beulah Nixon Wood on Jan. 20, 1916 on a ranch ju
2 CONC st south of Luling, Texas. He attended the one-room country Bethany School in Guadalupe County and later graduated from Luling High School and attended Southwest State Teachers College in San Marcos, Texas. He entered the U.S. Arm
2 CONC y Air Corps during World War II and served honorably with the 411th Squadron in the Aleutian Islands and elsewhere. His decorations include Aleutians Campaign Medal with Bronze Star, American Defense Service Medal and others. In 1
2 CONC 946, Gene went to work for Humble Oil and Refining Co. (later Exxon). He married the late Alice Miller Penton (deceased) and raised two sons. He retired in 1973, returning to his family ranch. He enjoyed the ranch life and working
2 CONC  with his cattle. In 1978, he met Elsie Bormann Bartoskewitz and they married in 1980. He was a member of H.U. Wood Post 245 of the American Legion and of the Exxon Retires Club. Gene was preceded in death by his parents; brothers
2 CONC  Kent Wood and Weldon Wood; sisters Louise Wood Ash, Fannie Wood Cheshire, Margie Wood Morris, Laura Wood Hancock, Julia Wood, Marie Schurig, and Merle Wood Young and his oldest son, James (Jim) A. Wood.* Reference: [https://www.f
2 CONC indagrave.com/memorial/68204926/gerald-gene-wood Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 26 2020, 21:24:23 UTC''
