1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''NOTE''' '''At Least 7 different men by the name of James Knox Walker ''' lived in Texas at the same time, they were not Capt. James Knox Walker, II nor his father James Knox Walker, I of Luling, Texas. The same 
2 CONC ages as father and son but were born, died, and lived in different areas. Although, ancestry trees have mixed the trees. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Particularly important not to mix these families, these men were all close in age. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Capt. James Knox Walker, II of Luling, Texas''' was born on April 16, 1882, in Guadalupe County, TX, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34765417429 James Knox Walker, Sr] and [https://www.geni.com/pro
2 CONC file-34765417421 Lucia Augusta Hamilton]. He was a Cattle and Horse Rancher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740807675 Alta Estelle Fisher] on November 5, 1902, in Caldwell, Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34765416884 Frances Hamilton Walker].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 26, 1905, in Luling, Caldwell County, TX, the United States from Consumption and was buried after in Luling City Cemetery, Luling, Caldwell, Texas, United States. 
