1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''James King Nixon''' was born on August 5, 1844, in Randolph, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-79564215 Zachariah Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925897 Gabriella Nixon]
2 CONC . He was a Texas rancher and farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064607 Mary Jane Little] on January 11, 1877. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064617 Thomas Preston Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064619 Edwin Homer Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064620 James Garrett Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064616 Buford King Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064621 Walton Derwood Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34743064622 Rhea Samuel Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 4, 1920, in Pearsall, Frio, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''*
2 CONT
2 CONT He migrated to Texas from Randolph County at some point after 1852 when his older brother's John T. Nixon and Capt. Robert Thomas Nixon of Luling and Old Nixon, Texas. They were raised in The Friends, Quaker Religion until they ca
2 CONC me to Texas. They didn't believe in Slavery and freed their slaves before the Civil War.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Early Nixon's of Texas" by Pat Ireland Nixon, MD, Genealogies by Dr. and Mrs. Pat Ireland Nixon, Jr., Published by Carl Hertzog, El Paso, Texas 1956
2 CONT
