1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Jesse H. Nixon''' was born in 1846 in Randolph County, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-79564215 Zachariah Nixon] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717925897 Gabriella Nixon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1861 in Val Verde, New Mexico, United States. during the Battle of Val Verde [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Valverde]
2 CONT
2 CONT Battle Next morning, February 21, Sibley sent an advance party consisting of four companies of the 2nd Texas Mounted Rifles under the command of Major Charles Pyron to scout ahead to the Valverde ford, with the 4th Texas Mounted R
2 CONC ifles under Lieutenant Colonel William Read Scurry following close behind. The rest of the brigade remained in the camp, intending to follow later.[12][13https://tshaonline.org/handbook/online/articles/qkf10
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Date	February – April 1862 Location	 New Mexico Territory Result	
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Union victory
2 CONT     Confederate retreat from New Mexico Territory
2 CONT     Confederate loss of Confederate Arizona Belligerents United States United States of America
2 CONT     New Mexico Territory
2 CONT     Colorado Territory
2 CONT ----
2 CONT  Confederate States of America
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Commanders and leaders Edward Canby Isaac Lynde	Henry Hopkins Sibley Thomas Green Strength 5,142	2,515[1] Casualties and losses ~166 killed, Jesse H. Nixon was one of them Killed during the Battle was reported to Captain Robert Th
2 CONC omas Nixon his older brother.  ~246 wounded, ~222 missing or captured	~400 killed or wounded, ~500 missing or captured[2]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Sibley's New Mexico Campaign His Older brother Captain Robert Thomas Nixon[https://www.geni.com/people/Captain-Robert-Nixon/6000000075592453259?through=6000000007645907506] was in The Texas Brigade. The Nixon family didn't believe
2 CONC  in slavery, were Democratic, born and raised in The Friends Society, Quaker Religion. The Nixon's feed their slaves in the 1830s, but when the Civil War broke out, they had to serve, Jesse H. Nixon's father sent him to Texas for 
2 CONC the older brother's to protect him, thinking Texas would be a safer place. Sadly, Jesse's destiny would be at The Battle of Val Verde and his young life ended. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Jesse H Nixon Age: 	18 Birth Date: 	abt 1843 Enlistment Date: 	1861 Military Unit: 	Fourth Cavalry (Fourth Mounted Volunteers, First Regiment, Sibley's Brigade)
2 CONT ----
