1 OCCU  Friends So. School Board Trustee
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT ''' Phineas Nixon III''' was born on January 13, 1796, in Back Creek, Randolph, North Carolina, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34683064081 Dr. Phinehas Nixon, I] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-795
2 CONC 63906 Millicent Nixon]. Friends Society School Board Trustee. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742664310 Esther Jones] on January 23, 1840, in New Garden Mh, Guilford Co., No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on May 9, 1845, in Back Creek Meeting, North Carolina, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Education'''
2 CONT Medical College in Philadelphia, PN. - [https://www.med.upenn.edu/ Perelman School of Medicine aka University of Pennsylvania ]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Marriage to Esther Jones - January 23, 1840
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000107334315844 Intention of Marriage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Opposed slavery, returned slaves to Haiti in 1826, many years before the Civil War.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/36333900/the_arkansas_gazette Dr. Phineas Nixon returned enslaved people of color on the ship St. Anne to Haiti in 1823]
2 CONT
2 CONT Believed in Equal Rights for People of Color  [https://www.newspapers.com/clip/36334186/the_society_of_friends_nc_1826/] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke University Library - https://divinityarchive.com/bitstream/handle/11258/11621/towardfreedomfor00hilt.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y[https://divinityarchive.com/bitstream/handle/11258/11621/towardfreedomfor00hilt.pdf?sequence=1&is
2 CONC Allowed=y Toward Freedom for All : North Carolina Quakers and Slavery]
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas and his wife Esther Jane Nixon (Jones) of Philadelphia gifted their home to the New Garden Boarding School.  Dr. Phineas Nixon, Jr. was one of the incorporators and the first trustee of the school and from 1835 to 1845, th
2 CONC e clerk of the Board of Trustees, their only officer. He was a very earnest and active friend of the infant school. He was "Chairman of the Committee on the Government of The Family."
2 CONT
2 CONT We have the Intention to Marry and the marriage of Esther Jones, names of her parents and siblings listed on meeting notes. Also The Friends Meeting of her entering The Meeting of Randolph County, NC  All documentation is attached
2 CONC . Her death date we have makes her 105 years old? will research.  make it circa.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference:
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.guilford.edu/who-we-are/friends-center/history]
2 CONT
2 CONT New Garden Boarding School was the early Guilford College of today.
2 CONT
