1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''A Pioneer Woman of Texas'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Susan Caroline "Carrie" Hysaw''' was married to a prominent rancher and landowner  Stephen Decatur Nixon on July 3, 1860, in Nixon, Guadalupe County, Texas. After several years, a few with him being away with Texas Mounted Calv
2 CONC ery fighting in the Civil War,  some working the land, horses and cattle, the birth of five children, he passed away in Paris, Texas, while on a cattle drive. Leaving her with the children she and Stephen had already moved in with
2 CONC  https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/111701831/person/430092071849/facts to assist him because his wife, Laura had passed away six months earlier.  After Stephen's death,   they continued to live with Robert Thomas Ni
2 CONC xon, even after his marriage to Frances Nixon (Andrews). She married a 2nd time but died three years later;  Carrie buried by her first husband, her children continued to live with Uncle Robert Thomas Nixon and his wife until they
2 CONC  were grown.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Susan Caroline Nixon (Hisaw)''' was born on January 15, 1841, in Rockbridge, Gwinnett, Georgia, USA, Rockbridge, Gwinnett, Georgia, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34757951110 James Monroe Hisaw] a
2 CONC nd [https://www.geni.com/profile-34757951105 Frances H Gordon]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Susan Caroline married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928407 Stephen Decatur Nixon] on July 3, 1860, in Texas, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928506 James A. Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928509 Stephen Maston Nixon, I]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928508 Adelaide S. Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928507 Frances Idella Nixon]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34717928511 Robert Fulton Nixon, Atty. I]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on May 22, 1875, in Nixon, Guadalupe County, Texas, USA, Guadalupe County, Texas, United States, and was buried in Old Nixon Cemetery, Nixon, Guadalupe, TX, United States at the young age of 34.
2 CONT ----
