1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Jean Marguerite Chandler (Champion)''' was born on March 27, 1920, in Los Angeles, California, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34748670125 Albert Nicholas Champion Md, II] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-3
2 CONC 4749483870 Winona Shanks Byington]. [1] She grew up in San Antonio, Texas where her father was a prominent physician and surgeon. She attended the prestigious private school St. Mary's Hall in San Antonio. She attended Mills Colle
2 CONC ge in Oakland, California,  graduated in 1942 with honors in English from The University of Texas, Austin and she was a member of the Kappa Kappa Gamma Sorority as well. During World War II she worked as a journalist with The San 
2 CONC Antonio Light Newspaper and was very active with the American Red Cross. She met her husband in 1942, while Dr. John Hughes Chandler  was stationed at Ft. Sam Houston in San Antonio with the Harvard Medical Battalion prior to his 
2 CONC military service during WWII. They married after he returned for serving. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They moved to Jackson, TN where Dr. Chandler became a founding member of The Jackson Clinic in 1950. Successful men have special women, such as Jean. She founded the Jackson Service League and was the first president. She was a me
2 CONC mber of The Junior League of San Antonio, Texas and later of Memphis, TN. Jean Champion assisted in establishing the West Tennessee Speech and Hearing Center as well as the first Girl Scout Headquarters in Jackson, TN. She was a m
2 CONC ember of the Episcopal Women's Altar Guild and the Episcopal Church Women. She did all of the above and raised four children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT As a young woman excelled in horseback riding, tennis, and diving.[ref[1]] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean married on July 9, 1945, in San Antonio, Texas [https://www.geni.com/profile-34749484327 John Hughes Chandler, MD]. Together they had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on November 19, 2009, in Fairhope, Baldwin, Alabama, USA and was buried in Ridgecrest Cemetery in Jackson, TN [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/135794006]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
