1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Still researching, Geni has NC as death, although the family at this time had moved to Wilkes County, GA and she died before her husband's Will was probated. 1823 in Wilkes County, Georgia, USA. She is not mentione
2 CONC d on the will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Jemina Stevens (Green)''' was born in 1750 in Baltimore, Baltimore, Maryland, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34669019368 Isaac Green, of Baltimore] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34681975374 Re
2 CONC becca Green]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemina married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532599 Edward Stevens] on November 5, 1795, in Liberty, Georgia. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532596 Elijah G Stevens]; [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/profile-34746801287 William J Stevens]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532597 Rutha Stevens]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532598 John W Stevens]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532600 Silas Stevens]; [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/profile-34761532601 Stephen B Stevens]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34761532604 Lucy Stevens]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died between 1797 and 1800 in North Carolina, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- '''References'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Her Father's lineage proven'''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Green-5252]  Children of Isaac Green and Rebecca :
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Shadrack Green.
2 CONT * 2. Isaac Green (Married Abigail Unknown).
2 CONT * 3. Meshack Green.
2 CONT * 4. Abednego Green.
2 CONT * 5. Hannah Green (Married Mr. Legit).
2 CONT * 6. Temperanice Green ? married? 
2 CONT * 7. Jemina Green - (Married Mr. Stevens).
2 CONT * 8. Belily Green (Married Walter Tebbit)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Isaac Green of Baltimore County
2 CONT
2 CONT dated 4 March 1797, proven 2 Aug 1800 
2 CONT
2 CONT I Isaac Green of Baltimore County and State of Maryland being of sound mind . . ..
2 CONT
2 CONT I  bequeath to my eldest son Shadrach Green the sum of 5 shillings and no more of my estate having given him all I intended.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I bequeath to my son Isaac Green my fulling mill with all ways and water courses.
2 CONT
2 CONT I bequeath to my three sons Meshach, Abednego and Isaac my dwelling  plantation containing about 95 acres in Baltimore Co to be equally divided between them except the fulling mill as here before devised.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Elijah Merryman all that part of my land before mentioned where the road now is leading from the said Merrymans Mill until it intersects the main road which passes by Mr. Burks and Mr. Nicholosons.
2 CONT
2 CONT To son Isaac my negro woman Sophia, also 2 bay colts, my dining table, chest of drawers, one bed and furniture thereunto belonging and one red cow with the increase thereof.
2 CONT
2 CONT To my four daughters Hannah Legit, Temperance  Green, Jermina Stevens, and Belily Tebitt all the residue part of my estate to be equally divided.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I appoint my son Isaac Green and Walter Tebett joint executors. Signed 4 March
2 CONT
2 CONT 1797
2 CONT
2 CONT  Isaac I-I-I Green
2 CONT
2 CONT  in the presence of
2 CONT
2 CONT James Hooker,
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Bosley,
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Merryman OF Benj.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed, Sealed, & Delivered In Presence of Ruth Franklin Thos. Franklin his mark John X Green
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Beware of transcription error made mentions 4 daughters, some copies skip Jermina and add Stevens to her sister Temperance's name.- The original will list all four daughters.    '''Isaac's Will is dated 1800. [Probate 2 Aug 1
2 CONC 800, written 4 March 1797]''' Isaac Green of Baltimore Co and State of MD being of sound mind . . ..I bequeath to my eldest son Shadrach Green the sum of 5 shillings and no more of my estate having given him all I intended. I bequ
2 CONC eath to my son Isaac Green my fulling mill with always and water courses. I bequeath to my three sons Meshach, Abednego and Isaac my dwelling plantation containing about 95 acres in Baltimore Co to be equally divided between them 
2 CONC except the fulling mill as here before devised. To Elijah Merryman all that part of my land before mentioned where the road now is leading from the said Merryman's Mill until it intersects the main road which passes by Mr. Burks a
2 CONC nd Mr. Nicholoson's. To son Isaac my negro woman Sophia, also 2 bay colts, my dining table, chest of drawers, one bed and furniture thereunto belonging and one red cow with the increase thereof. To my four daughters Hannah Legit, 
2 CONC Jermina Stevens, Temperance Green and Belily Tebitt (sic) all the residue part of my estate to be equally divided. I appoint my son Isaac Green and Walter Tebett (sic) joint executors. Signed 4 March 1797 Isaac Green in the presen
2 CONC ce of James Hooker, Charles Bosley, Nicholas Merryman of Benj. On the 2nd day of August 1800 came Isaac Green and Walter Tebett (sic) and testified. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes Adams-16917 14:36, 29 August 2016 (EDT)
2 CONT
2 CONT Land tract Pallas = Palace. Rebecca's death: after birth of Abednego and before Isaac's will as no mention of a wife in will. Charles b1792, sourced at FS of Isaac and Rebecca would have to be of another couple. an earlier Charles
2 CONC  Green mentioned in document re to Isaac: Maryland, Church Records, 1668-1995, database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F4ZF-6GZ : 24 February 2016), Isaac Green in entry for Charles Green, citing Christenin
2 CONC g, St. James' & St. Johns', Baltimore, Maryland, United States, various libraries, churches, historical and national societies, private and public records; FHL microfilm 14,451.
2 CONT
