1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Please Note''' Her middle name is James- she had a daughter named Martha Jane Lewis, please don't confuse and change. Look at her headstone- it clearly is written, '''Martha James Lewis''' 
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Martha James Lewis (Colvin)''' was born on July 17, 1819, in Culpeper, Virginia, USA, Culpeper, Culpeper County, Virginia, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-55670342 James C. Colvin] and [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/profile-126964283 Martha Polly Colvin]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married [https://www.geni.com/profile-89692250 Alfred Brown Lewis]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-90491831 Mary Columbia Lewis];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-90491852 Lizzie Lewis];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964659 Frances Lancaster (Lewis)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34740397494 Martha Jane Lewis]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She died on January 16, 1855, in Miami, Saline, Missouri, USA, Saline County, MO, the United States from Childbirth and was buried at The Miami Cemetery.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note: Many people confuse Alfred's wife's middle name as Jane, as per family records and genealogist research her correct name for her mother was Martha James Lewis (Colvin) - James being a family surname. They named a daug
2 CONC hter Mary Jane Lewis for a cousin Jane Ashby Smith who was visiting the family assisting with the birth and other children when Martha James Lewis (Colvin) died in childbirth - the baby was named Martha for the mother with the mid
2 CONC dle name of Jane. Jane Ashby Smith became the 2nd wife of Alfred Brown Lewis. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
