1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Dianna Field (Slaughter)''' was born circa 1799 in Of Fauquier Co., Virginia. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34660881116 Stanton Slaughter] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34660881146 Judith Steptoe Slaughter]
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dianna married [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964477 Henry Hill Field]. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737598 Henry Hill Field, Jr.]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737908 Stanto
2 CONC n Slaughter Field]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34742576418 Baby Field]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 19, 1838, in Irvington, Alabama, United States, and was buried in Field Family Burial Plat, Eufala, Fairview Cemetery, Eufaula, Barbour, Alabama, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She died on February 19, 1838, in Irvington, Alabama, United States.**
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Her husband, Henry Hill Field a successful merchant, and plantation owner,  while living in Alabama ran a sawmill. He moved with Diana Field (Slaughter) to Eufaula, Alabama, until her death, on February 19, 1838. He then moved bac
2 CONC k to Culpeper County, Virginia for several years. He sold his home in Eufaula he shared with his first her in 1842, **but in the deed, Mr. Field Reserved Ten Square Feet of the lot, which contained the graves of his Dianna Field (
2 CONC Slaughter) and her child. This plat became a part of the Fairview Cemetery, Eufaula,  Barbour County, Alabama. 
2 CONT
