1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT ''James Slaughter Field''' was born on February 19, 1838, in Eufaula, Barbour County, AL, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-126964477 Henry Hill Field] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34737737378 Dian
2 CONC na Field (Slaughter)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 19, 1838, in Eufala, Barbour, the United States from Died in Childbirth and was buried in Field Family Burial Plat. The child was buried with his mother.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT His father, Henry Hill Field a very successful merchant, and plantation owner, while living in Alabama ran a sawmill. He moved with his mother, Diana Field (Slaughter) to Eufaula, Alabama, until her death, on February 19, 1838. He
2 CONC  then moved back to Culpeper County, Virginia for several years. He sold his home in Eufaula he shared with his first wife in 1842, **but in the deed, Mr. Field Reserved Ten Square Feet of the lot, which contained the graves of hi
2 CONC s Dianna Field (Slaughter) and child. Which became the Fairview Cemetery, Eufaula, Barbour County, Alabama, US
