1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Susan Victorine Field''' was born on July 13, 1859, in Farmington, St Francois, Missouri, USA, Texas, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744229035 John Eubank Clardy] and [https://www.geni.com/profi
2 CONC le-34744229038 Lydia Ann Blanks]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Susan married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278435 William Edward Field] on June 17, 1879, in Farmington, Sankt Francois County, MO, United States. They met while he was attending the University of Missouri. Together they had
2 CONC  the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278626 Annie Russell Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278635 Sallie Bowen Ritchie (Field)];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278628 Margery Virginia Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278632 Willie Lynn Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278631 Edward Clardy Field];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278624 Susan Victorine Armentrout (Field)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT She died on May 22, 1923, in Austin, Travis County, TX, United States and was buried in Lockhart Municipal Burial Park, Lockhart, Caldwell, Texas, United States. [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39487720/susie-v-field[]]
2 CONT ---
2 CONT ---- She married William Edward Field June 17, 1879, she was the niece of ex-Congressman Martin Linn Clardy; the daughter of John Eubank Clardy and Lydia Ann Clardy (Banks) They had six children and resided in Lockhart, Caldwell C
2 CONC ounty, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The stained glass windows at the Emmanuel Episcopal Church has a plaque in the memory of Field Family name dedicated and donated by the Field family members. [(ref [http://www.eeclockhart.org/history.html F]
2 CONT
