1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Thomas McNeal''' was born on November 22, 1849, in Brenham, Washington County, Texas, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278891 William Wallace Mcneal] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-346782788
2 CONC 87 Elizabeth Walker Mcneal]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278434 Mary Virginia V McNeal]. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278512 Thomas Hill McNeal]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278519 W
2 CONC illiam Wallace McNeal]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278515 Edna Lea Fitzgerald]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278520 Lillie Tom Trigg]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34678278518 Mary Field McNeal]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 14, 1913, in Caldwell, Burleson County, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''' Thomas McNeal'''
2 CONT Full Name: Thomas McNeal
2 CONT Date of birth: November 22, 1849
2 CONT Date of death: February 14, 1913
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Legislation'''
2 CONT '''Terms of Service''' 
2 CONT Chamber	District	Dates of Service	Legislatures	Party	City/County	Note	Counties in District
2 CONT * H	86	Jan 14, 1913 - Feb 14, 1913	33rd (1)  	Democrat	Lockhart / Caldwell	 	Caldwell
2 CONT * H	60	Jan 10, 1911 - Jan 14, 1913	32nd  	Democrat	Lockhart / Caldwell	 	Caldwell
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Frank L. Tiller, sworn 3/17/1913, succeeded Thomas McNeal, died 2/14/1913. Members of the Texas Congress 1836-1845; Members of the Texas Legislature 1846-2004, 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Resolutions and Journal entries'''
2 CONT * 33rd Legislature, R.S., 2/24/1913, p. 666. Resolutions - Memorial.
2 CONT * Biographical Sketches
2 CONT * "Second Legislator Died Today from Spinal Meningitis" and "Will Try to Pass Katy Bill over Governor's Veto," 2/14/1913, p. 1. Reports on deaths of Thomas McNeal and Lee Killingsworth "of Longview" of meningitis. Denton Record-Ch
2 CONC ronicle.
2 CONT * "Legislative Halls Almost Forsaken . . . Death of Representative Hunt Shocking," 3/23/1913, p. 8; Obituary, "J.C. Hunt Dies in Austin: Representative from Randall County Had Been Ill Since Feb. 15 - His Is Fourth Death This Sess
2 CONC ion," 3/23/1913, p. 10. Cause of death: cerebro-spinal meningitis; other members who died "succumbing to the same disease" were Representatives Neal [sic: McNeal], Killingsworth, and Kelly [sic: Kelley]. Galveston Daily News.
2 CONT * Obituary, Thomas McNeal. "Hon. Thos. M'Neal Dies; A Victim of Meningitis (Second Representative to Die within 24 hours)", 2/15/1913, p. 4. Mentions death of Lee Killingsworth "of Longview" of meningitis. Galveston Daily News.
2 CONT * Memorial services and tributes for Thomas McNeal, J.C. Hunt, Lee Killingsworth, and D.C. Kelley, including biographical sketches - 33rd Legislature, Sunday, 3/23/1913, pp. 1469-1485. D.C. Kelley born in 1856, p. 1475. House Jour
2 CONC nal.
2 CONT * Report describing memorial services on the deaths of Representatives McNeal, Killingsworth, Kelley, and Hunt, 3/24/1913, p. 2. San Antonio Light.
2 CONT
