2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary Gonzales Inquirer Feb. 11, 1960
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Fritzgerald Funeral Wednesday 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Wednesday at 3 p.m. from the Seydler Funeral home for Mrs. A. H. Fitzgerald, who died at the Holmes Memorial hospital at 10:30 a.m. Tuesday following a long period of ill health.
2 CONT She had fallen and broken her hip several months ago and had been confined to her bed since that time. She was 82.
2 CONT The deceased was born in Luling on January 28, 1878. The former Edna McNeal, she was married on October 31, 1900, to A. H. Fitzgerald who preceded her in death June of 1954.
2 CONT She was the daughter of Thomas and Mary Virginia Field McNeal.
2 CONT Survivors include a daughter, Mrs. J. E. Lawley, this city; a granddaughter, Mrs. J. R. Tinsley, Jr., and three great-grandchildren, Carolyn, Jimmy and John Tinsley, all of Gonzales.
2 CONT Other survivors include two sisters, Mrs. W. B. Trigg of Lockhart and Mrs, Mary Carter of Nixon.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/80359922/edna-lee-fitzgerald Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects
