2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Rebecca Trigg (Bingham)''' was born in 1795 in Albemarle County, VA, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722379927 George Washington Bingham] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722379961 Louisa Bing
2 CONC ham (Vest)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34746309017 Wyatt Bingham] on July 12, 1812, in Albemarle, Virginia. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715937591 Rebecca Wyatt Trigg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After her mother-in-law, https://www.geni.com/people/Priscilla-Bingham/6000000176120131833,  and daughter passed away in 1851, her son-in-law soon re-married. Her first cousin, https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-George-Bingham-USA/6
2 CONC 000000080591455968?through=6000000080589578768 sent for her to assist him with his young children, she lived with his family until she died in 1870 in St. Louis, Missouri and she was buried in his burial area.  
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Her husband's Will is attached, she's named, and her daughter Rebecca Wyatt Trigg, as well. executor was her son-in-law, https://www.geni.com/people/John-Trigg/6000000075571370894?through=6000000075571284907  [https://www.geni.com
2 CONC /documents/view?doc_id=6000000113734512854]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrow Rock, Saline County, Mo. History and the Bingham Family [https://arrowrock.org/about-discover-arrow-rock/] In 1968, the home of artist George Caleb Bingham was listed separately as a National Historic Landmark. Arrow Rock is
2 CONC  also a certified site on the Lewis & Clark and Santa Fe Trails. Wyatt was https://www.geni.com/people/Capt-George-Bingham-USA/6000000080591455968, USA first cousin, and his wife's nephew. Rebecca and Wyatt were of Bingham lineage
2 CONC , Uncle and Aunt.
2 CONT
