1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Jane Hendrick Kleine (O'Neal)''' was born on April 13, 1916, in Shreveport, Caddo Parish, LA, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34764815198 Benjamin Franklin O'Neal, Sr] and [https://www.geni.com/pro
2 CONC file-34764815203 Susan Abernathy O'Neal]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34722670397 Colonel Bingham Trigg Kleine] on January 14, 1937, in Shreveport, Caddo, Louisiana, USA. Two children were born and survive. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Silent Ranks'''
2 CONT
2 CONT I wore no uniforms, no blues or greens.
2 CONT
2 CONT But I was in the military, I was in the ranks rarely seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT I was not in the chain of command; orders I did not give or get.
2 CONT
2 CONT But my husband was the one who did, This I never forgot.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am not the one who fired a weapon. Who put his life on the line.
2 CONT
2 CONT My husband was a patriot, a brave and pride filled man.
2 CONT
2 CONT And the call to serve his country not all can understand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Behind the lines, he saw things needed to this keep this country free.
2 CONT
2 CONT My husband made the sacrifice, but so do our children and me.
2 CONT
2 CONT I loved the man I married; the military was his life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I pledged to support my hero and stood ranks among the silent ranks known as,
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Military Wife'''
2 CONT
2 CONT author unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on May 30, 1999, in Shreveport, Caddo, Louisiana, USA, and was buried after in Forest Park East Cemetery, Shreveport, Caddo Parish, Louisiana, USA. * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103974926/jane-hendrick
2 CONC -kleine Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 10 2020, 8:47:56 UTC''
2 CONT ----
