1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Margaretta Drusilla Lancaster (LeGrand)''' was born on April 19, 1769, in Prince Edward, Virginia, Colonial America, Prince Edward, VA, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-17346136 Alexander, LeGrand, 
2 CONC Sr.] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-59993400 Lucy LeGrand]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaretta married [https://www.geni.com/profile-2751812 John Lancaster, IV Of Clover Forest Plantation] on March 17, 1789, in Prince Edward, Virginia, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721583 Nathaniel Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721581 Judith Baker Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-2748086 John Alexander Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721582 William LeGrand Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721580 Samuel C Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721584 Nancy Alexander Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721585 Elizabeth LeGrand Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721586 Thomas Crawford Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34756721587 Emeline B Lancaster];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964807 Josiah Lancaster]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on December 14, 1825, in Clover Forest, Prince Edward, Virginia, United States, and was buried in Clover Forest Plantation Cemetery. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=yale.39002004723855&view=1up&seq=15] Historic Homes by Robert A. Lancaster, .; grandson of John Lancaster and Margaretta Drucilla Lancaster (Legrand). '''Clover Forest Plantation''' In Princ
2 CONC e Edward County, which is separated by the Appomattox River from what we called the "Upper James" section, is a unique homestead which was for many years the property of the Lancaster Family, while across the Appomattox is Clover 
2 CONC Forest, another quaint old home of the Lancasters. Both of these homes were built when the prevailing type of home was the log-cabin and was doubtless then looked upon as considerable mansions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Clover Forest was the home of John Lancaster, a native of Prince Edward County, Virginia. He died on January 28, 1826, and was buried at Clover Forest where he sleeps also with his wife, Drucilla, daughter of Alexander LeGrand
2 CONC , who died on December 14, 1825, and Lucy Walker, his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT John A. Lancaster ( son of John and Drucilla Lancaster) moved to Richmond, in 1813, and later became the first president of the first railroad in Virginia, "The Richmond, Fredericksburg & Potomack, Rail Road." He was the father of
2 CONC  Robert A. Lancaster, a prominent businessman of Richmond, VA, and author of this book.  Of Prince Edward County
2 CONT ==Biography==
