1 NAME Thompson Mason /Rector/ I
2 GIVN Thompson Mason
2 SURN Rector
2 NSFX I
2 _MARNM Rector
1 NAME Thomas Mason Rector I
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Manor, Travis County, Texas, United States of America
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 NOV 1801
2 PLAC Sevier County, Tennessee, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 FEB 1892
2 PLAC Travis County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
3 CITY Caldwell
3 STAE Texas
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Atty., Rancher
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Various members of the Rector family were prominent and actively involved in the formation and growth of Manor, Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Thomson Mason (T. M.) Rector, Sr., was born in 1801 in Sevier County, TN. About 1821, he married Miss Wilson, who died shortly after. After studying law, at the age of 21 he was admitted to the bar and opened an office in Be
2 CONC llefonte, AL. where he was later elected and served for a number of years as Jackson County Judge..
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1831, he married a wealthy widow, Lucy Ann Hudson Lancaster, with whom he had five children
2 CONT In 1853, they were one of the last members of his family to leave Alabama. He sold his wife's land and his land, and they moved to Texas, settling in Travis County. With the combined wealth of the Hudson/Baker and Lancaster inheri
2 CONC tances, his wife brought considerable wealth into the marriage; with it, they built a successful ranch and farm, so successful that he never returned to practicing law.  Before his wife died in 1867, he arranged for her two childr
2 CONC en from her first marriage to receive equal shares in her estate,  but before his death, all land was transferred directly to his natural sons, so her two children born to Josiah Lancaster didn't receive their part of the Lancaste
2 CONC r, Hudson, and Baker inheritance. Her children were named as sole heirs of Josiah Lancaster's estate, and they were named in the Hudson. Baker probates as well, in which they never received their inheritance. Thompson Mason Rector
2 CONC  made sure all was transferred directly to the Rector children before his death.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1858, as a Master Mason, he was a founding member of Parsons Masonic Lodge #222, which met on the upper floor of the Parsons Female Seminary.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1863, he was appointed, along with 6 other leading citizens, to the Board of Trustees of the Parsons Female Seminary. Two years later, he was listed as President of the Board.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judge Rector died February 19, 1892, at the age of 90, and was buried in Rector Cemetery located on his plantation, along with Lucy Ann, who had passed away in 1867 at the age of 64.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Judge Rector’s namesake, Thomson Mason Rector, Jr. was born on October 10, 1838 in 
2 CONT Jackson County, AL., and moved to Travis County with the family in 1853. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as a member of Company D, Eighth Texas Cavalry, better known as Terry's Texas Rangers, during the Civil War and was active in reunions of the Terry's Texas Rangers Association as late as the year before he passed away. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, since the newly-formed town of Manor had not yet organized a fire department, when his house caught fire on May 6, 1875, it burned to the ground. An Austin newspaper carried this story:[https://manorstories.blogspot
2 CONC .com/2019/02/the-rectors.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Thomas Mason Rector''' was born on November 14, 1801, in Sevier, Tennessee. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-43987048 Benjamin Rector] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-54134737 Sarah Rector]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thompson married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964803 Lucy Ann Lancaster (Hudson)] in 1831 in Bellefonte, Alabama. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964897 Catherine Elizabeth Rector];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725328546 Benjamin Fieldon Rector];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964904 Thompson Mason Jr. Rector, Planter];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964896 Lucy Jane Rector];
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725328549 Landoria Madaline Rector]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thompson married [https://www.geni.com/profile-49795246 Miss Wilson] in 1821 in Sevier, Tennessee. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on February 19, 1892, in Caldwell, Burleson County, Texas, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
