1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain John Hudson  Not in DAR- have documentation from Family Bibles, Probated Wills, and Military record he was a Captain, and served in the Military, but not the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Captain John Hudson''' was born in 1771 in Prince Edward County, Virginia, Colonial America. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-58822942 Lieutenant William Hudson] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-31059443 Mary Fra
2 CONC nces Hudson]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964891 Lucy Hudson] on June 5, 1790, in Prince Edward County, Virginia, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-128673397 Elizabeth D Flood]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964894 Caleb Baker Hudson]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964889 John Hudson]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964893 Nathaniel Hudson]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964803 Lucy Ann Lancaster (Hudson)]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964890 William Hudson]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on July 7, 1840, in  Bellefonte, Jackson County, Alabama, United States., buried in Bellefonte Cemetery. 
2 CONT ---
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
