1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 AUG 1866
2 PLAC Manor, Travis, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT When Isaac Wildbahn was born on June 23, 1817, in Marion, Ohio, his father, Johannes, was 43 and his mother, Catherine, was 35. He married Ann Drucilla Lancaster in 1850 in Bellefonte, Jackson, Alabama. He was a large landowner in
2 CONC  Jackson County, Alabama and in 1853 they sold their land and with her inheritance from the sale of her father's land they moved to Manor, Travis County, Texas. He built a large plantation near Manor, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Windbahn Plantation was a working ranch and farm with several thousand acres. Isaac Wildbahn bred horses and cattle as well as successful mercantile stores in Travis County, Texas. He fought for The Texas Calvary during the Civil 
2 CONC War and died on August 25, 1866, at age 51 yrs old and just three years after their move,  when they were finally getting settled, The fencing was finished, their large home was built, five children born, but  one died as an infan
2 CONC t and two lost to illness.  Now Ann Drucilla faces another loss her beloved husband. She never does not marry again, he left her financially secure and she was independently minded and was able to manage quite well.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Isaac Wildbahn''' was born on June 25, 1815, in Marion County, Ohio, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac ''''''married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964811 Ann Drucilla Wildbahn] in 1850 in Jackson, Alabama. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578852 Katherine Rector Townes (Wildbahn)]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578874 Ann Parsons Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578883 Frank Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578917 Lucy H Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578955 John Edgar Wildbahn]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578891 Ernest Wildbahn]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on August 25, 1866, in and is buried Rector Cemetery, Manor, Travis, Texas, USA.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''References.''' The Rector Cemetery was The Rector Plantation at one time, now a Golf Course. The owners fenced off the cemetery and locked the gate. [http://www.austintxgensoc.org/cemeteries/rector-cemetery/]
2 CONT
