1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Katherine Rector Townes''' Kate Wildbahn's husband was a Judge and law professor. From 1907 until his death in 1923 he was dean of the School of Law at the University of Texas. Townes Hall, a law building on the UT campus, is n
2 CONC amed for Judge Townes. She was busy socially with Junior League and various charities. She changed moved her membership from Episcopalian to The University Baptist Church. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Katherine Rector Townes''' was born on January 17, 1853, in Jackson County, Alabama, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34716578807 Isaac Wildbahn] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34715964811 Ann Druscilla Wi
2 CONC ldbahn]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591836 John Charles Townes, Sr] in 1872. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591840 Ernest Wildbahn Townes];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591839 Eggleston D. Townes];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591838 Edgar E Townes];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591842 Anna Cousins Townes];
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34744591841 John Charles Townes, Jr].
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on June 4, 1915, in and was buried in Austin, Travis County, Texas, USA. Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/42686559/kate-townes Find A Grave Memorial] - 
