1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Yvonne Claire Lancaster''' was born on February 1, 1927, in Houston, Harris, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34725329063 Frank Huston Lancaster, MD] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34763942126 Maida
2 CONC  Ezzell]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yvonne married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34763942327 Raymond Severs Clark] on July 12, 1945, in San Antonio, Bexar, Texas, USA. Together they had three children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34763942338 Lloyd Ray Clark]; [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/profile-34763942336 Loren Jay Clark]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34763942335 David Lee Clark]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yvonne C. Clark, 89, of Edmond, OK, went home to be with her Heavenly Father Sunday, February 7, 2016. She was known most of her life as Sugar by family, friends, and coworkers. She was buried in Liberal, Seward County, Kansas, Un
2 CONC ited States of America.  She was born on February 1, 1927, to Dr. Frank and Maida Lancaster in Houston, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 15, 1945, she married Raymond S. Clark in San Antonio, Texas. He preceded her in death on April 7, 2007. She and Raymond made their home in Liberal from 1949 until 2012 when Sugar moved to Bradford Village Retirement Commu
2 CONC nity in Edmond, Oklahoma.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was Water Safety Director for the American Red Cross from 1950 until 1969, and she was a reading aide at West and South Junior High School from 1970 until 1990. She also volunteered for many years with Boy Scouts acting as Den
2 CONC  Mother and in other capacities, earning several awards for her service. Sugar is survived by three sons, daughter-in-law, and one granddaughter
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/158414291/yvonne-c-clark Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 23 2020, 9:39:08 UTC''
