1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Armour Lee Fulbright''' was born on August 8, 1916 in Hebbronville, Jim Hogg County, Texas, USA. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34767140250 Robert Hinnant] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34767139340 Lucy Armo
2 CONC ur Heppenstall]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Armour married [https://www.geni.com/profile-53446255 John Earl (7) Fulbright] in 1936. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on April 23, 2011, in Texas, USA and was buried in Greenhill Cemetery, Hebbronville, Jim Hogg County, Texas, USA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Armour Lee Hinnant Fulbright was born August 8, 1916, in Hebbronville, Texas, to Robert and Lucy Armour Heppenstall Hinnant. She graduated from Hebbronville High School in 1933. She attended Westmoreland College in San Antonio (no
2 CONC w Trinity University) and Texas A&I College (now Texas A&M University – Kingsville). She married Jack Fulbright in 1936. She was preceded in death by her husband J.E. "Jack" Fulbright, parents, and infant brother. She is survived 
2 CONC by her son Robert (Agnes Dee) Fulbright of Hebbronville and granddaughters Leslee (Garret) Brandt of Basalt, Colorado, and Vicki (Chris) Calwell of Durango, Colorado. She is also survived by four great-grandchildren: Robert Steven
2 CONC son Brandt, Katherine Fulbright Brandt, Jennifer Huanxun Brandt and Julianne FuJun Brandt, all of Basalt, Colorado.
2 CONT
2 CONT Armour was an avid reader. Up until the last decade of her life, she read three newspapers daily and worked the crossword puzzles in each one. She enjoyed reading magazines as well but her favorite genre by far was a good mystery-
2 CONC suspense novel. Armour's distinct experiences include celebrating nearly all her life milestones in the home her parents built in 1915: birth, marriage, and both 50th and 60th wedding anniversaries. Armour was also a lifelong memb
2 CONC er of the First United Methodist Church of Hebbronville.  Funeral services will be held Tuesday, April 26 at 10:00 a.m. in the First United Methodist Church of Hebbronville, with burial following at Green Hill Cemetery. 
2 CONT
